  "raw": {
    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/phd-position-using-microfluidics-to-observe-and-manipulate-coacervate-droplets-2327/?lang=en": {
      "title": "PhD position Using microfluidics to observe and manipulate coacervate droplets",
      "description": "PhD position Using microfluidics to observe and manipulate coacervate droplets - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts PhD position Using microfluidics to observe and manipulate coacervate droplets Apply now PhD PhD position Using microfluidics to observe and manipulate coacervate droplets This vacancy is only available in English We are looking for a 4-year PhD candidate to join our nationally funded, multi-partner research consortium, Towards De-Novo Life. The main aim of this interdisciplinary project is to achieve minimal life based on chemical rather than biological components such as DNA, proteins or other macromolecules. Our PhD candidate will contribute by developing new microfluidic tools to work with micrometer-sized coacervate droplets, the compartments in which chemical replication, growth and evolution will take place. Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 12 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time 1 FTE €3.204 - €4.051 Share this vacancy PhD position Using microfluidics to observe and manipulate coacervate droplets Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/phd-position-using-microfluidics-to-observe-and-manipulate-coacervate-droplets-2327/?lang=en What are you going to do? The de-novo synthesis of life requires integrating the essential features of life, which include replication (the ability to copy oneself), metabolism (promoting the formation of one’s own components from material in the environment) and compartmentalization (keeping the internal components together and separate from the environment) into a system that is maintained out of equilibrium. Key to the creation of a minimal form of life is Darwinian evolution of the resulting synthetic cell-like systems. Serving as the compartments in our work are coacervate microdroplets, consisting of a very dense aqueous phase containing a high concentration of macromolecules. Because coacervates can exist in dilute aqueous phases without loss of droplet structure, they can act as cell-like spheres without the need of a membrane to contain their content. In this project, you will use microfluidics to create a first-generation platform to achieve growth and division of micrometer-sized coacervate droplets. You will then consider populations of coacervate droplets confined in a second, more complex microfluidic platform, monitoring their growth and mutation rates. “Mother” droplets will be followed alongside their “daughters” using fluorescence microscopy, with addition of precursor materials (“nutrients”) and random removal of individuals (“death”). Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 12 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time €3.204 - €4.051 Who are you? We are looking for someone who meets the following qualifications: Essential qualifications MSc degree in Biomedical Engineering, Physical or Analytical Chemistry, or related disciplines Demonstrated hands-on experience with microfabrication and microfluidics Experience with fluorescence imaging Enthusiasm, self-motivation, creativity, and team spirit Ability to work in a multidisciplinary environment Excellent communication skills in English (verbal and written) Preferred qualifications Programming skills (Python, MATLAB, or similar) for data analysis Ability to design and implement microcontroller-based control systems (Arduino, Raspberry Pi, etc.) Experience with synthetic organic chemistry What can you expect from us? In accordance with the collective labor agreement for Dutch universities, we offer a salary of at least €                    3.204\n                    \n                    up to a maximum of €                    4.051                    (promovendus)\n                    gross per month for a full-time employment contract. 232 vacation hours per year, based on a 38-hour workweek (1.0 FTE). You can also work more or fewer hours in exchange for more or fewer free hours. For example, with a 40-hour workweek, you save 96 extra free hours, and with a 36-hour workweek, you lose 96 hours. End-of-year bonus of 8.3% and 8% holiday allowance. Extensive opportunities for personal and professional development. A temporary full-time (1.0 FTE) position for one year at first with the option of renewal for another three years. Where will you be working? At the University of Groningen (UG), researchers from all fields of academia and technology are working on academic challenges and societal questions. Lecturers prepare their students for meaningful careers within or outside the academic world. Interdisciplinary research and teaching, sharing of knowledge, collaboration with businesses, government institutions, and societal organizations are aspects that are of the utmost importance to this European top university. The UG aims to be an open academic community with an inclusive and safe working climate that invites you to add your value. The Faculty of Science and Engineering (FSE) provides teaching and research across a wide range of disciplines, from physics and biology to artificial intelligence, mechanical engineering, and pharmacy. In close collaboration with partners from industry, healthcare, and society, we contribute to the urgent challenges of our time, such as energy, sustainability, digitization, and medical technology. Our community is open and informal, with more than 7,000 students, 1,000 PhD students, and 1,400 staff members from all over the world. If you would like to learn more about the Faculty of Science and Engineering, visit rug.nl/fse . You will join the Groningen Research Institute of Pharmacy (GRIP), which is positioned within FSE, and is physically located within the University Medical Centre Groningen (UMCG) of the Faculty of Medical Sciences (FMS). Pharmaceutical research within GRIP is multidisciplinary and bridges clinical and biomedical sciences on the one hand, and chemistry, mathematics, engineering, and physics on the other. The interaction between the pharmaceutical sciences with these fundamental and clinical sciences offers excellent opportunities for cutting-edge research. string(27) \"sollicitatieprocedure_wp_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n  }\n} Application procedure Step 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Step 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Step 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Step 4: Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture. Step 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen! Interested? Does this vacancy appeal to you? If so, click on the button below and apply straightaway. Please add the following documents to your application: CV. Cover letter. Statement of purpose. Transcripts BSc and MSc degree. Contact information for 3 references. Apply now Do you have any questions or need more information? Questions about the content of the job? Elisabeth Verpoorte Full Professor E.M.J.Verpoorte@rug.nl Questions about your application process? Elisabeth Verpoorte Full Professor E.M.J.Verpoorte@rug.nl Information about applying When scheduling meetings, we will take your schedule into account as much as possible. The University of Groningen considers social safety important. We strive to be a university where staff and students feel respected and at home, regardless of differences in background, experiences, perspectives, and identity. For more information, see also our page about our diversity policy . Acquisition is not appreciated. Our selection procedure follows the guidelines of the NVP Application Code. Read document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Go straight to All vacancies Working at UG Contact information University of Groningen PO Box 72 9700 AB Groningen The Netherlands How to find us Follow us on array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
    },
    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/phd-position-in-neuromorphic-computing-fpga-design-and-hardware-acceleration-2348/?lang=en": {
      "title": "PhD position in Neuromorphic Computing, FPGA Design, and Hardware Acceleration",
      "description": "PhD position in Neuromorphic Computing, FPGA Design, and Hardware Acceleration - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts PhD position in Neuromorphic Computing, FPGA Design, and Hardware Acceleration Apply now PhD PhD position in Neuromorphic Computing, FPGA Design, and Hardware Acceleration This vacancy is only available in English Are you excited about designing the next generation of energy-efficient AI hardware? Do you want to contribute to cutting-edge research at the intersection of neuromorphic computing, computer architecture, and hardware acceleration? The University of Groningen is seeking a highly motivated PhD candidate to join the international QuNeCo project, a collaborative research initiative between leading universities in the Netherlands and Japan. As part of an interdisciplinary team, you will develop novel neuromorphic computing architectures inspired by the human brain to enable future heterogeneous computing systems with unprecedented energy efficiency and performance. This PhD position offers the opportunity to collaborate with internationally renowned researchers, publish in leading conferences and journals, and gain experience in architecture design, hardware implementation, FPGA prototyping, and AI applications. Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 31 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time 1 FTE €3.204 - €4.051 Share this vacancy PhD position in Neuromorphic Computing, FPGA Design, and Hardware Acceleration Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/phd-position-in-neuromorphic-computing-fpga-design-and-hardware-acceleration-2348/?lang=en What are you going to do? As a PhD candidate, you will contribute to the design and development of next-generation neuromorphic computing systems through algorithm–hardware co-design and computing-in-memory technologies. Your research will span the complete hardware design flow, from architectural exploration to hardware prototyping and experimental evaluation. Project website: Home | QuNeCo Your responsibilities include: Designing novel neuromorphic computing architectures based on application requirements and heterogeneous computing use cases. Investigating emerging memory technologies, including SRAM, RRAM, MRAM, and FeRAM, for efficient neuromorphic hardware implementations. Developing RTL implementations of neuromorphic architectures using hardware description languages and validating their functionality through simulation. Evaluating performance, energy efficiency, and scalability using industry-standard electronic design automation (EDA) tools. Developing representative AI and neuromorphic applications to demonstrate the proposed architectures. Prototyping hardware accelerators on FPGA platforms and integrating them into heterogeneous computing systems. Performing comprehensive experimental evaluations and publishing research findings in leading international conferences and journals. Collaborating closely with project partners in the Netherlands and Japan and participating in international project meetings, workshops, and research visits. Contributing to teaching activities and supervising Bachelor’s and Master’s students where appropriate. Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 31 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time €3.204 - €4.051 Who are you? We are looking for an enthusiastic researcher who enjoys solving challenging problems and working in an international research environment. You should have: A Master’s degree in Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Computer Science, Embedded Systems, or a closely related field. A strong background in computer architecture and digital hardware design. Experience with hardware description languages such as Verilog, SystemVerilog, or VHDL. Familiarity with FPGA development or RTL design methodologies. Knowledge of computer architecture, hardware accelerators, AI hardware, or neuromorphic computing. Programming experience in Python and/or C/C++. Experience with EDA tools (e.g., Cadence, Synopsys, Vivado) is considered an advantage. Interest in emerging memory technologies and computing-in-memory architectures is desirable. Excellent English communication skills, both written and spoken. Strong analytical abilities, creativity, and the motivation to conduct independent research while collaborating within an international team. What can you expect from us? In accordance with the collective labor agreement for Dutch universities, we offer a salary of at least €                    3.204\n                    \n                    up to a maximum of €                    4.051                    (promovendus)\n                    gross per month for a full-time employment contract. 232 vacation hours per year, based on a 38-hour workweek (1.0 FTE). You can also work more or fewer hours in exchange for more or fewer free hours. For example, with a 40-hour workweek, you save 96 extra free hours, and with a 36-hour workweek, you lose 96 hours. End-of-year bonus of 8.3% and 8% holiday allowance. Extensive opportunities for personal and professional development. A full-time position (1.0 FTE). The successful candidate will first be offered a temporary position of one year with the option of renewal for another three years. Prolongation of the contract is contingent on sufficient progress in the first year to indicate that a successful completion of the PhD thesis within the next three years is to be expected. A PhD training programme is part of the agreement, and the successful candidate will be enrolled in the Graduate School of Science and Engineering.\nTeaching: Employed PhD candidates are expected to spend 10% of their working hours on teaching and/or supervising students. Where will you be working? At the University of Groningen (UG), researchers from all fields of academia and technology are working on academic challenges and societal questions. Lecturers prepare their students for meaningful careers within or outside the academic world. Interdisciplinary research and teaching, sharing of knowledge, collaboration with businesses, government institutions, and societal organizations are aspects that are of the utmost importance to this European top university. The UG aims to be an open academic community with an inclusive and safe working climate that invites you to add your value. The Faculty of Science and Engineering (FSE) provides teaching and research across a wide range of disciplines, from physics and biology to artificial intelligence, mechanical engineering, and pharmacy. In close collaboration with partners from industry, healthcare, and society, we contribute to the urgent challenges of our time, such as energy, sustainability, digitization, and medical technology. Our community is open and informal, with more than 7,000 students, 1,000 PhD students, and 1,400 staff members from all over the world. If you would like to learn more about the Faculty of Science and Engineering, visit rug.nl/fse . The successful candidate will join the Bernoulli Institute for Mathematics, Computer Science and Artificial Intelligence within the Faculty of Science and Engineering at the University of Groningen . The research will be carried out in the Innovative Computer Architecture group. The group of Dr. Farhad Merchant conducts internationally recognized research on computing-in-memory architectures, neuromorphic computing, hardware security, and energy-efficient computer systems. The candidate will become part of the QuNeCo project, an ambitious collaboration between universities in the Netherlands and Japan that aims to develop next-generation heterogeneous computing platforms by combining emerging hardware technologies with novel computing paradigms. The position provides extensive opportunities for international collaboration, research visits, interdisciplinary training, and interaction with leading academic researchers across the consortium. string(27) \"sollicitatieprocedure_wp_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n  }\n} Application procedure Step 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Step 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Step 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Step 4: Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture. Step 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen! Interested? Does this vacancy appeal to you? If so, click on the button below and apply straightaway. Please add the following documents to your application: Motivation letter (maximum 2 pages). Curriculum Vitae. Academic transcripts (BSc and MSc). Contact details of two academic referencesCopy of MSc thesis (or a representative publication, if available). Apply now Do you have any questions or need more information? Questions about the content of the job? Farhad Merchant Assistant Professor f.a.merchant@rug.nl Questions about your application process? Farhad Merchant Assistant Professor f.a.merchant@rug.nl Information about applying When scheduling meetings, we will take your schedule into account as much as possible. The University of Groningen considers social safety important. We strive to be a university where staff and students feel respected and at home, regardless of differences in background, experiences, perspectives, and identity. For more information, see also our page about our diversity policy . Acquisition is not appreciated. Our selection procedure follows the guidelines of the NVP Application Code. Read document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Go straight to All vacancies Working at UG Contact information University of Groningen PO Box 72 9700 AB Groningen The Netherlands How to find us Follow us on array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
    },
    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/three-phd-positions-in-ml-guided-directed-evolution-2341/?lang=en": {
      "title": "Three PhD positions in ML-guided directed evolution",
      "description": "Three PhD positions in ML-guided directed evolution - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts Three PhD positions in ML-guided directed evolution Apply now PhD Three PhD positions in ML-guided directed evolution This vacancy is only available in English Are you passionate about combining the directed evolution of diverse biomolecules with deep learning approaches and contributing to the development of better (bio)catalysts and drugs? We are offering three fully-funded, 4-year PhD positions at the University of Groningen or the Technical University of Eindhoven. Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 15 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time 1 FTE €3.204 - €4.051 Share this vacancy Three PhD positions in ML-guided directed evolution Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/three-phd-positions-in-ml-guided-directed-evolution-2341/?lang=en What are you going to do? Evolution is an all-purpose problem solver, which researchers mimic in the laboratory to engineer tailor-made (bio)molecules that aid us in combating diseases and in realizing a sustainable economy. While effective, such directed evolution campaigns are not only laborious and time-consuming, but also cover only a miniscule fraction of the unimaginably large sequence space available. As a result, means to guide evolutionary trajectories along a biomolecule’s fitness landscape are sought-after, as they could greatly accelerate evolutionary searches. Within the framework of the recently funded ML-GUIDE project, we will make directed evolution guidable and, ultimately, predictable by machine learning. Specifically, you will build a first-in-class framework to expedite the design of high-affinity binders that engage with therapeutic targets or efficient (bio)catalysts for synthetic applications. By seamlessly merging cutting-edge directed evolution, next-generation sequencing, and deep learning approaches, you will establish accelerated Design-Build-Test-Learn cycles to continuously improve models via active learning and guide evolutionary trajectories toward promising but otherwise inaccessible sequence spaces. You will be embedded in one of the three research groups involved in the ML-GUIDE project and focus your efforts on guiding engineering efforts for one particular biomolecule and its associated function. (1) Dr. Robert Pollice ( https://pollicegroup.web.rug.nl/ ) leads the Artificial Organic Chemistry Lab at the University of Groningen and will supervise a project focusing on developing efficient peptide catalysts for powerful C-C-bond forming reactions. (2) Prof. Francesca Grisoni ( https://molecularmachinelearning.com/ ) leads the Molecular Machine Learning Group at the Technical University Eindhoven and will lead a project on designing potent cyclic-peptide drugs for therapeutic intervention. (3) Prof. Clemens Mayer ( https://mayerlab.nl/ ) leads the Molecular Evolution Group at the University of Groningen and will tackle a project on making the directed evolution of biocatalysts predictable by machine learning. As part of the ML-GUIDE team, you will closely collaborate with researchers to identify commonalities and distinct aspects of engineering biomolecules for diverse applications! The preferred starting date is between 01-11-2026 and 01-03-2026 . Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 15 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time €3.204 - €4.051 Who are you? We are looking for creative, motivated, and determined candidates, who meet the following requirements: An MSc degree (or an equivalent university degree) in (Bio)chemistry, Biotechnology, Computational Chemistry, Synthetic Chemistry/Biology or a related field. Experience in one of the following areas is highly preferred: directed evolution, molecular machine learning, next-generation sequencing, or synthetic chemistry. An interest in working as part of a highly interdisciplinary team at the interface of synthetic biology, molecular machine learning, and synthetic chemistry. A research-oriented attitude with good analytical skills. Excellent communication and organization skill. What can you expect from us? In accordance with the collective labor agreement for Dutch universities, we offer a salary of at least €                    3.204\n                    \n                    up to a maximum of €                    4.051                    (promovendus)\n                    gross per month for a full-time employment contract. 232 vacation hours per year, based on a 38-hour workweek (1.0 FTE). You can also work more or fewer hours in exchange for more or fewer free hours. For example, with a 40-hour workweek, you save 96 extra free hours, and with a 36-hour workweek, you lose 96 hours. End-of-year bonus of 8.3% and 8% holiday allowance. Extensive opportunities for personal and professional development. Promovendus: 1 year + 3 year Where will you be working? At the University of Groningen (UG), researchers from all fields of academia and technology are working on academic challenges and societal questions. Lecturers prepare their students for meaningful careers within or outside the academic world. Interdisciplinary research and teaching, sharing of knowledge, collaboration with businesses, government institutions, and societal organizations are aspects that are of the utmost importance to this European top university. The UG aims to be an open academic community with an inclusive and safe working climate that invites you to add your value. The Faculty of Science and Engineering (FSE) provides teaching and research across a wide range of disciplines, from physics and biology to artificial intelligence, mechanical engineering, and pharmacy. In close collaboration with partners from industry, healthcare, and society, we contribute to the urgent challenges of our time, such as energy, sustainability, digitization, and medical technology. Our community is open and informal, with more than 7,000 students, 1,000 PhD students, and 1,400 staff members from all over the world. If you would like to learn more about the Faculty of Science and Engineering, visit rug.nl/fse . The University of Groningen is a research university, currently in or around the top 100 on several influential ranking lists. The Faculty of Science and Engineering (FSE) is the largest faculty within the University, offering first-rate education and research in a wide range of science and engineering disciplines. In this position, you would be embedded in the Stratingh Institute for Chemistry . Eindhoven University of Technology is an internationally top-ranking university in the Netherlands that combines scientific curiosity with a hands-on attitude. Our spirit of collaboration translates into an open culture and a top-five position in collaborating with advanced industries. Fundamental knowledge enables us to develop innovative solutions to complex societal challenges. In this position, you would be embedded in the Institute for Complex Molecular Systems and in the Eindhoven AI Systems Institute . string(27) \"sollicitatieprocedure_wp_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n  }\n} Application procedure Step 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Step 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Step 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Step 4: Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture. Step 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen! Interested? Does this vacancy appeal to you? If so, click on the button below and apply straightaway. Please add the following documents to your application: A letter stating (1) your motivation to apply, (2) your key qualities relevant for this position, and (3) which research group in the ML-GUIDE consortium you would like to join. An up-to-date curriculum vitae. Diplomas (BSc and Msc (if available)) and transcript of records. Contact information of two academic references. Apply now Do you have any questions or need more information? Questions about the content of the job? Clemens Mayer Associate Professor C.Mayer@rug.nl Questions about your application process? Clemens Mayer Associate Professor C.Mayer@rug.nl Information about applying When scheduling meetings, we will take your schedule into account as much as possible. The University of Groningen considers social safety important. We strive to be a university where staff and students feel respected and at home, regardless of differences in background, experiences, perspectives, and identity. For more information, see also our page about our diversity policy . Acquisition is not appreciated. Our selection procedure follows the guidelines of the NVP Application Code. Read document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Go straight to All vacancies Working at UG Contact information University of Groningen PO Box 72 9700 AB Groningen The Netherlands How to find us Follow us on array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
    },
    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/technisch-specialist-gbs-applicatiebeheer-engineering-1994/?lang=en": {
      "title": "Technisch Specialist GBS – Applicatiebeheer & Engineering",
      "description": "Technisch Specialist GBS – Applicatiebeheer & Engineering - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts Technisch Specialist GBS – Applicatiebeheer & Engineering Apply now Technisch Specialist GBS – Applicatiebeheer & Engineering This vacancy is only available in Dutch Ben jij de technische spil achter onze gebouwautomatisering omgeving? Heb jij een scherp analytisch oog voor complexe systemen en weet jij als geen ander de brug te slaan tussen operationele technologie en IT? Dan zoeken wij jou. University Services 0.8 - 1 FTE €3.873 - €4.925 Share this vacancy Technisch Specialist GBS – Applicatiebeheer & Engineering Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/technisch-specialist-gbs-applicatiebeheer-engineering-1994/?lang=en Wat ga je doen? Je borgt dat de GBS-omgeving technisch correct functioneert, stabiel is, aansluit op IT-kaders en overdraagbaar is. Concreet betekent dit: Analyseren en doorgronden van de GBS-omgeving als geheel; van applicatielaag tot koppelingen met regeltechniek. Technisch oplossen van storingen binnen de systemen: je duikt in de diepte, vindt de oorzaak en borgt een structurele oplossing. Implementeren van wijzigingen en ondersteuning bij migraties en upgrades van de GBS-systemen. Beheer en afstemming van koppelingen met regeltechniek en andere systemen in de gebouwomgeving. Afstemming met de IT-afdeling (CIT) over infrastructuur, security en integratie-eisen. Zorgdragen voor heldere documentatie en informatie in een overdraagbare omgeving zodat kennis geborgd blijft. Adviseren van de organisatie over technische vraagstukken rondom gebouwautomatisering. Wat jij niet doet: functioneel beheer, IT-infrastructuurbeheer, uitvoerend onderhoud en assetmanagement. Jouw focus ligt puur op de technische laag van de GBS-applicatie en haar integraties. Resultaten van jouw werk: Stabiele en goed functionerende GBS-systemen die de gebouwen, gebruikers en processen optimaal ondersteunen. Structurele oplossingen voor storingen en technische vraagstukken — geen lapmiddelen. Een goed geïntegreerde IT/OT-omgeving, in nauwe samenwerking met CIT en gebouwgebonden installaties en systemen. Overdraagbare systemen en up-to-date documentatie/informatie die de continuïteit waarborgen. University Services €3.873 - €4.925 Wie ben jij? Als Technisch Specialist GBS ben je verantwoordelijk voor de technische werking, samenhang en doorontwikkeling van de GBS-applicatie en haar koppelingen. Je werkt binnen het team Dagelijks beheer & monitoring (DB&M) als de cruciale schakel tussen OT en IT in een van de grootste universitaire vastgoedportefeuilles van Nederland. Voor deze rol zoeken we een enthousiaste collega die: MBO+/HBO werk- en denkniveau, bij voorkeur in de richting van klimaatregeltechniek, elektrotechniek, gebouw automatisering, of informatica. Aantoonbare ervaring met GBS-systemen, je kent de omgeving van binnenuit. Kennis van BACnet/IP en vergelijkbare protocollen, inclusief: opbouw van BACnet-objecten en datapunten communicatie tussen veldniveau (DDC) en GBS netwerkstructuren en segmentatie binnen OT-omgevingen interpretatie van storingen en afwijkingen in datacommunicatie Analytisch sterk: je doorgrondt complexe systemen, legt verbanden en lost problemen structureel op. Je bent zelfstandig en proactief, je pakt relevante vraagstukken op zonder dat je daarvoor gevraagd hoeft te worden. Verbindend tussen disciplines: je schakelt moeiteloos tussen techniek, IT en organisatie. Kennis van aanverwante systemen zoals energiemonitoring, beveiligingsinstallaties of BI-tooling is een pré. Waarom zoek jij ons? Complexiteit die uitdaagt: de RUG beheert een omvangrijke, veelzijdige vastgoedportefeuille in het hart van Groningen met grootschalige gebouwautomatisering die altijd door moet draaien. Techniek én impact: jouw werk draagt direct bij aan een veilige, duurzame en optimale omgeving voor tienduizenden studenten en medewerkers. Samenwerking op hoog niveau: je werkt nauw samen met de assetmanagers systemen en klimaatregelinstallaties, de IT-afdeling (CIT) en programma’s zoals Smart Buildings of projecten. Ruimte voor ontwikkeling: uitstekende scholingsfaciliteiten en volop kansen om jouw expertise verder te verdiepen en te verbreden. Wat kan je van ons verwachten? Wij bieden, in overeenstemming met cao Nederlandse Universiteiten een salaris van minimaal €                    3.873\n                                          (schaal 09)                    \n                    tot maximaal €                    4.925                    (salary scale 10.7)\n                    bruto per maand bij een fulltime dienstverband. 232 verlofuren per jaar, o.b.v. een 38-urige werkweek (1.0 fte). Je kunt ook meer of minder uren werken, in ruil voor meer of minder vrije uren. Zo spaar je bij een 40-urige werkweek 96 extra vrije uren en lever je bij een 36-urige werkweek 96 uur in. Eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3% en 8% vakantietoeslag. Uitgebreide mogelijkheden voor persoonlijke en professionele ontwikkeling. Een tijdelijke functie van 0,8 tot 1,0 fte voor periode van één jaar. Waar ga je werken? Bij de Rijksuniversiteit Groningen (RUG) werk je bij een brede topuniversiteit, met aandacht voor alle takken van wetenschap en techniek. Ondersteunende medewerkers leveren een essentiële bijdrage aan de inzet van docenten en onderzoekers voor de ontwikkeling van talent en een betere, duurzame samenleving. De RUG wil een open academische gemeenschap zijn met een inclusief en veilig werkklimaat dat je uitnodigt om jouw waarde toe te voegen. University Services (US) is an engaged organization with over 1,250 staff members. Every day, we dedicate ourselves to creating an inspiring and sustainable academic environment in which students and staff can grow, collaborate, and reach their full potential. We support teaching, research, and operations in a progressive and collaborative way. From property maintenance to supporting the Board of the University, we proudly fulfil an important role at the University of Groningen as a facilitating and advisory service. Our services are wide-ranging and reach across the entire University. We work closely with faculties and other service units to support them as effectively as possible. If you would like to learn more about University Services, visit our website . Je komt te werken op de afdeling Vastgoedbeheer & Onderhoud, onderdeel van de Vastgoedorganisatie binnen University Services van de Rijksuniversiteit Groningen. Je rapporteert aan de Teamleider DB&M en werkt nauw samen met assetmanagement (AM-AO), functioneel beheer en de IT-afdeling (CIT). string(24) \"sollicitatieprocedure_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(69) \"Second interview and possible assessment and/or requesting references\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(145) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. This interview can be complemented with an assessment. We may also ask for references at this point.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(455) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\r\n\r\nCurious about what the onboarding process at the University of Groningen looks like? On our information page for new employees , you can read what to expect.\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(69) \"Second interview and possible assessment and/or requesting references\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(145) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. This interview can be complemented with an assessment. We may also ask for references at this point.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(455) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\r\n\r\nCurious about what the onboarding process at the University of Groningen looks like? On our information page for new employees , you can read what to expect.\"\n  }\n} Sollicitatieprocedure Stap 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Stap 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Stap 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Stap 4: Second interview and possible assessment and/or requesting references We may schedule a second interview with you. This interview can be complemented with an assessment. We may also ask for references at this point. Stap 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\r\n\r\nCurious about what the onboarding process at the University of Groningen looks like? On our information page for new employees , you can read what to expect. Interesse? Klinkt dit als een uitdaging die bij je past? Solliciteer dan direct via onderstaande knop! Voeg bij je sollicitatie de volgende documenten toe: CV. Motivatiebrief. Solliciteer nu Heb je vragen of meer informatie nodig? Heb je vragen over de inhoud van de vacature? Rick van der Wal Beleidsmedewerker rick.van.der.wal@rug.nl Heb je vragen over de sollicitatieprocedure? Berber Thasing HR-adviseur b.thasing@rug.nl Informatie over solliciteren Bij de planning van de gesprekken houden wij zoveel mogelijk rekening met jouw agenda. De Rijksuniversiteit Groningen vindt sociale veiligheid belangrijk. We streven ernaar een universiteit te zijn waar medewerkers en studenten zich gerespecteerd en thuis voelen, ongeacht verschillen in achtergronden, ervaringen, perspectieven en identiteit. Voor meer informatie zie ook onze pagina over ons diversiteitsbeleid . Acquisitie wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Onze selectieprocedure volgt de richtlijnen van de NVP Sollicitatiecode Lees hier het document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Jump to Alle vacatures Werken bij RUG Contactinformatie Rijksuniversiteit Groningen Postbus 72 9700 AB Groningen Waar vindt u ons Volg ons op array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
    },
    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/senior-beheerder-ict-microsoft-client-platform-1745/?lang=en": {
      "title": "Senior Beheerder ICT",
      "description": "Senior Beheerder ICT - Microsoft Client platform - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts Senior Beheerder ICT - Microsoft Client platform Apply now Senior Beheerder ICT - Microsoft Client platform This vacancy is only available in Dutch Word jij enthousiast van moderne Microsoft-werkplekken die altijd beschikbaar, veilig en up-to-date moeten zijn in een omgeving waar technologie, onderwijs en onderzoek samenkomen? Bij het Centrum voor Informatie Technologie (CIT) van de Rijksuniversiteit Groningen (RUG) – één van de oudste en meest innovatieve universiteiten van Nederland – zoeken wij een Senior Beheerder ICT – Microsoft Client platform met technische diepgang, overzicht en een passie voor end-user computing. Als senior specialist speel jij een sleutelrol in het ontwerpen, beheren en doorontwikkelen van onze werkplekvoorzieningen voor duizenden studenten en medewerkers. Je krijgt ruimte om te verbeteren, te automatiseren en richting te geven, binnen een team waar hard wordt gewerkt én gelachen. Wil jij bijdragen aan betrouwbare en toekomstbestendige digitale werkplekken voor onderwijs en onderzoek? Kom ons Endpoint & Servermanagement team versterken! Centrum voor Informatie Technologie 1 FTE €3.706 - €6.682 Share this vacancy Senior Beheerder ICT - Microsoft Client platform Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/senior-beheerder-ict-microsoft-client-platform-1745/?lang=en Wat ga je doen? Als Senior Beheerder ICT – Microsoft Client platform maak je deel uit van het Endpoint & Servermanagement team van het CIT. Dit team is verantwoordelijk voor het beheer en de doorontwikkeling van endpoints, werkplekken en onderliggende Microsoft-technologie. Je richt je primair op het beheer en de verdere professionalisering van onze fysieke en virtuele werkplekken, die intensief worden gebruikt binnen onderwijs, onderzoek en bedrijfsvoering. Je werkt in een complexe, dynamische omgeving waar stabiliteit, security, standaardisatie en gebruikerservaring centraal staan. Taken & verantwoordelijkheden: Beheren en optimaliseren van circa 13.000 fysieke werkplekken en diverse virtuele werkplekken. Ontwerpen, implementeren en beheren van het Microsoft Client platform (Windows 10/11). Beheer en doorontwikkeling van endpoint management via Microsoft Intune en MECM/SCCM. Oplossen van complexe incidenten en verstoringen (2e en 3e lijns). Analyseren van structurele problemen en doorvoeren van verbeteringen. Coördineren van werkzaamheden binnen het team en het domein. Opstellen van voorstellen voor proces- en platformverbeteringen. Doorvoeren van wijzigingen met oog voor security, stabiliteit en gebruikersimpact. Adviseren van stakeholders binnen het CIT over werkplekontwikkelingen. Documenteren van configuraties, processen en standaarden. Actief volgen en toepassen van nieuwe ontwikkelingen binnen end-user computing. Centrum voor Informatie Technologie €3.706 - €6.682 Wie ben jij? Je werkt graag aan een duidelijke visie op moderne werkplekken en krijgt energie van het verbeteren en stabiliseren van complexe omgevingen. Je combineert technische expertise met een proactieve, collegiale houding. Jij brengt mee: Hbo-werk- en denkniveau . Minimaal 7 jaar ervaring in een vergelijkbare functie. Ruime ervaring met Windows 11 en Windows Server 2019/2022/2025. Ruime ervaring met Microsoft Intune en MECM/SCCM. Ervaring met profile management tooling zoals FSLogix en ProfileUnity. Ruime ervaring met Microsoft Azure waaronder AVD (Azure Virtual Desktop). Ervaring met virtuele werkplekken zoals Citrix VDI (XenDesktop), SBC (XenApp), PVS en MCS is een pre. Bekend met thin client omgevingen zoals IGEL, Dell Wyse, HP Thin Clients en/of ATRUST is een pre. Ervaring met Agile werken is een pre. Goede beheersing van de Nederlandse en Engelse taal. Bereidheid om deel te nemen aan een rooster voor consignatie-/beschikbaarheidsdiensten. Aantoonbare ervaring met security hardening , audits en compliance. Aantoonbare ervaring met het inrichten en beheren van omgevingen middels Infrastructure as Code (IaC) en Configuration as Code (CaC). Zeer goede Powershell-vaardigheden . Ervaring met CI/CD (Azure DevOps). Ervaring met monitoring en proactief beheer. Technieken die je kent of graag wilt leren: Applicatiemanagement zoals App-V, MSIX, Liquit, FlexApp(One) en/of App Layering . Verdere automatisering en standaardisatie binnen het endpoint-domein. Nieuwe ontwikkelingen binnen de end-user computing markt. TerraForm en/of OpenTofu. Microsoft Graph API. En verder: Je bent analytisch, zorgvuldig en neemt initiatief. Je werkt graag samen en deelt je kennis. Je vindt het leuk om – als het zo uitkomt – ook mee te denken of bij te springen richting AD & Windows Server Beheer (pre, geen vereiste). Je voelt je thuis in een Agile-omgeving (of wilt dat graag worden). Humor wordt gewaardeerd. Sterker nog: die hebben we hier ook. Maak je geen zorgen als je niet álles al beheerst – motivatie, leergierigheid en teamfit vinden wij minstens zo belangrijk. Hier word jij blij van: Bijdragen aan de verdere ontwikkeling van de werkplekarchitectuur. Het bouwen aan een veilige, moderne en toekomstbestendige werkplek. Het oplossen van complexe vraagstukken en structurele verbeteringen. Samenwerken in een team waar professionaliteit en humor hand in hand gaan. Ruimte om te experimenteren met en leren van nieuwe technologieën. Wat kan je van ons verwachten? Wij bieden, in overeenstemming met cao Nederlandse Universiteiten een salaris van minimaal €                    3.706\n                                          (salary scale 10)                    \n                    tot maximaal €                    6.682                    (salary scale 11)\n                    bruto per maand bij een fulltime dienstverband. 232 verlofuren per jaar, o.b.v. een 38-urige werkweek (1.0 fte). Je kunt ook meer of minder uren werken, in ruil voor meer of minder vrije uren. Zo spaar je bij een 40-urige werkweek 96 extra vrije uren en lever je bij een 36-urige werkweek 96 uur in. Eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3% en 8% vakantietoeslag. Uitgebreide mogelijkheden voor persoonlijke en professionele ontwikkeling. Een dienstverband voor bepaalde tijd voor de duur van 1 jaar, dat daarna bij goed functioneren kan worden omgezet naar een dienstverband voor onbepaalde tijd. Waar ga je werken? Bij de Rijksuniversiteit Groningen (RUG) werk je bij een brede topuniversiteit, met aandacht voor alle takken van wetenschap en techniek. Ondersteunende medewerkers leveren een essentiële bijdrage aan de inzet van docenten en onderzoekers voor de ontwikkeling van talent en een betere, duurzame samenleving. De RUG wil een open academische gemeenschap zijn met een inclusief en veilig werkklimaat dat je uitnodigt om jouw waarde toe te voegen. The Center for Information Technology (CIT) at the University of Groningen supports and facilitates academic research and university education through high-quality data and IT solutions, advice, and training. Our mission is Teaching and research: supported by innovative and reliable IT services . With over 300 staff members, we manage the University’s IT infrastructure and supporting processes. To effectively support the strategic objectives of the University on a daily basis, we work in a customer-oriented way with self-organizing teams in the areas of Teaching, Research, Organizational Systems, Basic Workplaces, and Infrastructure. Our core values are excellence, expertise, and customer orientation. If you would like to learn more about the Center for Information Technology, visit rug.nl/cit . Het Endpoint & Servermanagement team beheert samen met het Microsoft Beheerteam de volledige Microsoft-stack voor circa 33.000 studenten en 6.500 medewerkers. We werken Agile, geven ruimte aan initiatief en waarderen humor. Meer weten? Kijk op https://www.rug.nl/cit Kom jij ons team versterken? string(24) \"sollicitatieprocedure_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(69) \"Second interview and possible assessment and/or requesting references\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(145) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. This interview can be complemented with an assessment. We may also ask for references at this point.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(455) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\r\n\r\nCurious about what the onboarding process at the University of Groningen looks like? On our information page for new employees , you can read what to expect.\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(69) \"Second interview and possible assessment and/or requesting references\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(145) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. This interview can be complemented with an assessment. We may also ask for references at this point.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(455) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\r\n\r\nCurious about what the onboarding process at the University of Groningen looks like? On our information page for new employees , you can read what to expect.\"\n  }\n} Sollicitatieprocedure Stap 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Stap 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Stap 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Stap 4: Second interview and possible assessment and/or requesting references We may schedule a second interview with you. This interview can be complemented with an assessment. We may also ask for references at this point. Stap 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\r\n\r\nCurious about what the onboarding process at the University of Groningen looks like? On our information page for new employees , you can read what to expect. Interesse? Klinkt dit als een uitdaging die bij je past? Solliciteer dan direct via onderstaande knop! Voeg bij je sollicitatie de volgende documenten toe: CV. Motivatiebrief. Voor deze functie wordt een Verklaring Omtrent Gedrag gevraagd. Solliciteer nu Heb je vragen of meer informatie nodig? Heb je vragen over de inhoud van de vacature? Gert Jan Verweij Engineering and application manager g.j.verweij@rug.nl Heb je vragen over de sollicitatieprocedure? Raoul Terlaak Afdelingshoofd R.G.Terlaak@rug.nl Informatie over solliciteren Bij de planning van de gesprekken houden wij zoveel mogelijk rekening met jouw agenda. De Rijksuniversiteit Groningen vindt sociale veiligheid belangrijk. We streven ernaar een universiteit te zijn waar medewerkers en studenten zich gerespecteerd en thuis voelen, ongeacht verschillen in achtergronden, ervaringen, perspectieven en identiteit. Voor meer informatie zie ook onze pagina over ons diversiteitsbeleid . Acquisitie wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Onze selectieprocedure volgt de richtlijnen van de NVP Sollicitatiecode Lees hier het document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Jump to Alle vacatures Werken bij RUG Contactinformatie Rijksuniversiteit Groningen Postbus 72 9700 AB Groningen Waar vindt u ons Volg ons op array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
    },
    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/projectleider-installatietechniek-1451/?lang=en": {
      "title": "Projectleider Installatietechniek",
      "description": "Projectleider Installatietechniek - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts Projectleider Installatietechniek Apply now Projectleider Installatietechniek This vacancy is only available in Dutch Ben jij een doortastende organisator met een passie voor techniek en vastgoed? Krijg jij energie van het aansturen van complexe onderhouds- en bouwprojecten, waarin kwaliteit, samenwerking en resultaat centraal staan? Wil jij bijdragen aan toekomstbestendig vastgoed binnen een toonaangevende universiteit? Dan zoeken wij jou als projectleider Vastgoed bij de Rijksuniversiteit Groningen (RUG)! Vastgoed en Investeringsprojecten 0.8 - 1 FTE €3.706 - €5.760 Share this vacancy Projectleider Installatietechniek Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/projectleider-installatietechniek-1451/?lang=en Wat ga je doen? Als projectleider ben jij de drijvende kracht achter grote onderhouds- en faculteitsprojecten. Jij bereidt projecten zorgvuldig voor, organiseert ze soepel en begeleidt ze van begin tot eind. Als aanspreekpunt voor alle betrokkenen houd jij het overzicht en communiceer je helder met alle partijen. Je bewaakt het budget, de kwaliteit en de voortgang van het project en stuurt bij wanneer nodig. Daarnaast geef je vanuit jouw expertise advies om projecten succesvol af te ronden. Vastgoed en Investeringsprojecten €3.706 - €5.760 Wie ben jij? We zoeken een enthousiaste collega met: Hbo werk- en denkniveau, opgedaan door relevante werkervaring en/of opleidingen in de richting van werktuigbouwkunde, meet- en regeltechniek, installatietechniek, of soortgelijk. Aantoonbare werkervaring als projectleider in een technische projectomgeving Sterke organisatorische vaardigheden en het vermogen om overzicht te houden en waar nodig bij te sturen. Goede communicatieve vaardigheden, een groot gevoel van verantwoordelijkheid en eigenaarschap, en een resultaatgerichte instelling. Affiniteit met elektrotechniek, wat als pre wordt gezien. Wat kan je van ons verwachten? Wij bieden, in overeenstemming met cao Nederlandse Universiteiten een salaris van minimaal €                    3.706\n                                          (salary scale 10)                    \n                    tot maximaal €                    5.760                    (schaal 10)\n                    bruto per maand bij een fulltime dienstverband. 232 verlofuren per jaar, o.b.v. een 38-urige werkweek (1.0 fte). Je kunt ook meer of minder uren werken, in ruil voor meer of minder vrije uren. Zo spaar je bij een 40-urige werkweek 96 extra vrije uren en lever je bij een 36-urige werkweek 96 uur in. Eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3% en 8% vakantietoeslag. Uitgebreide mogelijkheden voor persoonlijke en professionele ontwikkeling. het betreft een tijdelijke aanstelling voor 1 jaar met uitzicht op een aanstelling voor onbepaalde tijd. Waar ga je werken? Bij de Rijksuniversiteit Groningen (RUG) werk je bij een brede topuniversiteit, met aandacht voor alle takken van wetenschap en techniek. Ondersteunende medewerkers leveren een essentiële bijdrage aan de inzet van docenten en onderzoekers voor de ontwikkeling van talent en een betere, duurzame samenleving. De RUG wil een open academische gemeenschap zijn met een inclusief en veilig werkklimaat dat je uitnodigt om jouw waarde toe te voegen. University Services (US) is an engaged organization with over 1,250 staff members. Every day, we dedicate ourselves to creating an inspiring and sustainable academic environment in which students and staff can grow, collaborate, and reach their full potential. We support teaching, research, and operations in a progressive and collaborative way. From property maintenance to supporting the Board of the University, we proudly fulfil an important role at the University of Groningen as a facilitating and advisory service. Our services are wide-ranging and reach across the entire University. We work closely with faculties and other service units to support them as effectively as possible. If you would like to learn more about University Services, visit our website . De Vastgoedorganisatie is onderdeel van het cluster Campus & Community, dat op zijn beurt deel uitmaakt van University Services (US). University Services is een betrokken organisatie met ruim 1.250 medewerkers. We zetten ons elke dag in voor een inspirerende en duurzame academische omgeving waar studenten en medewerkers kunnen groeien, samenwerken en het beste uit zichzelf halen. We ondersteunen onderwijs, onderzoek & impact en bedrijfsvoering op een vooruitstrevende en verbindende manier. Van vastgoedonderhoud tot ondersteuning van het College van Bestuur: we vervullen met trots een belangrijke rol binnen de RUG als faciliterende en adviserende dienst. Onze dienstverlening is veelzijdig en raakt bijna elke hoek van de universiteit. We werken nauw samen met faculteiten en andere diensten om hen zo goed mogelijk te faciliteren. Afdeling Vastgoedprojecten is verantwoordelijk voor de realisatie van alle nieuwbouw- en verbouwprojecten en het groot onderhoud van de vastgoedportefeuille van de RUG. Daarnaast voert de afdeling kleine exploitatieprojecten uit. Dit zijn aanpassingen in de gebouwen vanuit de faculteiten en de diensten. De projecten variëren van zeer grote nieuwbouwprojecten tot kleine(re) projecten bij faculteiten. Bij de afdeling zijn circa 30 projectleiders en projectmedewerkers werkzaam. string(24) \"sollicitatieprocedure_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(69) \"Second interview and possible assessment and/or requesting references\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(145) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. This interview can be complemented with an assessment. We may also ask for references at this point.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(455) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\r\n\r\nCurious about what the onboarding process at the University of Groningen looks like? On our information page for new employees , you can read what to expect.\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(69) \"Second interview and possible assessment and/or requesting references\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(145) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. This interview can be complemented with an assessment. We may also ask for references at this point.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(455) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\r\n\r\nCurious about what the onboarding process at the University of Groningen looks like? On our information page for new employees , you can read what to expect.\"\n  }\n} Sollicitatieprocedure Stap 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Stap 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Stap 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Stap 4: Second interview and possible assessment and/or requesting references We may schedule a second interview with you. This interview can be complemented with an assessment. We may also ask for references at this point. Stap 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\r\n\r\nCurious about what the onboarding process at the University of Groningen looks like? On our information page for new employees , you can read what to expect. Interesse? Klinkt dit als een uitdaging die bij je past? Solliciteer dan direct via onderstaande knop! Voeg bij je sollicitatie de volgende documenten toe: Cv, motivatiebrief Solliciteer nu Heb je vragen of meer informatie nodig? Heb je vragen over de inhoud van de vacature? Ritske Tuinstra Projectmanager r.k.tuinstra@rug.nl Heb je vragen over de sollicitatieprocedure? Ritske Tuinstra Projectmanager r.k.tuinstra@rug.nl Informatie over solliciteren Bij de planning van de gesprekken houden wij zoveel mogelijk rekening met jouw agenda. De Rijksuniversiteit Groningen vindt sociale veiligheid belangrijk. We streven ernaar een universiteit te zijn waar medewerkers en studenten zich gerespecteerd en thuis voelen, ongeacht verschillen in achtergronden, ervaringen, perspectieven en identiteit. Voor meer informatie zie ook onze pagina over ons diversiteitsbeleid . Acquisitie wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Onze selectieprocedure volgt de richtlijnen van de NVP Sollicitatiecode Lees hier het document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Jump to Alle vacatures Werken bij RUG Contactinformatie Rijksuniversiteit Groningen Postbus 72 9700 AB Groningen Waar vindt u ons Volg ons op array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
