    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/phd-position-data-science-2465/?lang=en": {
      "title": "PhD position Data Science",
      "description": "PhD position Data Science - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts PhD position Data Science Apply now PhD PhD position Data Science This vacancy is only available in English Are you interested in using data science to understand how digital measures can capture clinically meaningful aspects of reward, motivation and impulsivity? Do you want to develop and apply innovative digital proxies and combine them with neurobiological markers to advance precision medicine across mental and metabolic health conditions? Then this PhD position in an international pioneering project may be an excellent opportunity for you. You will work in an interdisciplinary, international research project aiming to advance a transdiagnostic precision-medicine framework centred on Reward, Motivation and Impulsivity. The project brings together expertise in longitudinal research, biomarker discovery, clinical validation, data science, evidence synthesis and stakeholder engagement. A central ambition is to move beyond disease-specific approaches by identifying biological, behavioural and digital markers that can help characterise clinically meaningful processes across different health conditions. As a PhD candidate, you will contribute to this ambition by helping establish the evidence base for digital proxies, developing and applying data-driven measures, and investigating their relationships with neurobiological markers. Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 30 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time 1 FTE €3.204 - €4.051 Share this vacancy PhD position Data Science Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/phd-position-data-science-2465/?lang=en What are you going to do? We are looking for an ambitious and analytically minded PhD candidate to investigate digital proxies of Reward, Motivation and Impulsivity (RM&I) and their relationship with neurobiological markers and clinically relevant outcomes. Your work will be connecting systematic evidence synthesis, data science, longitudinal research and clinical validation. Your research will contribute to understanding whether and how digital measures can provide scalable and meaningful proxies for RM&I-related processes across major depressive disorder (MDD), Alzheimer’s disease (AD), and obesity (OB) . Your PhD research will have three closely connected components: Systematic review of digital proxies: You will systematically synthesise existing evidence on digital proxies relevant to RM&I, identifying the types of digital measures that have been investigated, their relationship with behavioural and clinical constructs, and their potential relevance for transdiagnostic research. Development and application of digital proxies: You will use data-science approaches to develop, characterise and/or evaluate RM&I-related digital proxies. You will subsequently apply these digital proxies to analyses conducted within the project’s longitudinal and clinical datasets, contributing to the identification of meaningful patterns across individuals and disease trajectories. Hypothesis testing with neurobiological markers: You will investigate relationships between digital proxies and neurobiological markers, testing hypotheses about the biological mechanisms underlying RM&I-related processes. Depending on the available data and the development of the research, this may involve integrating digital, behavioural, clinical and neurobiological measures. An important aspect of your work will be to examine the clinical and transdiagnostic relevance of digital proxies. You will contribute to determining whether digital measures can complement existing biomarkers and endpoints and help identify measurable features of RM&I that are relevant across different conditions. You will work closely with researchers involved in longitudinal cohort analyses, clinical studies, biomarker research and evidence synthesis. Your work will therefore sit at the intersection of data science, digital phenotyping, clinical research and neurobiology . Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 30 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time €3.204 - €4.051 Who are you? We are looking for a motivated researcher with a strong interest in data science, digital proxies, biomarkers and clinical research. You have: A completed Master’s degree in a relevant field such as data science, artificial intelligence, computer science, neuroscience, psychology, biomedical sciences, medicine, epidemiology, health sciences or a related discipline. A strong interest in applying quantitative and computational approaches to biomedical or clinical research. Experience with statistical analysis and/or data science. Programming experience, preferably in R and/or Python. An interest in digital phenotyping, digital biomarkers, behavioural data or other digital measures. The ability to critically assess and synthesise scientific literature. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. Good scientific writing and communication skills. The ability to work independently while contributing effectively to an interdisciplinary team; and Excellent written and spoken English. Experience with one or more of the following would be an advantage: Systematic reviews or evidence synthesis. Longitudinal or cohort data analysis. Multimodal or multi-omics data. Machine learning or other data-science methods. Digital phenotyping or development of digital biomarkers/proxies. Neuroimaging, electrophysiology or other neurobiological measures. Behavioural or cognitive measures. Reproducible research and open-science practices; and Research involving MDD, AD, obesity, RM&I or related transdiagnostic constructs. We particularly value candidates who are curious about how digital measures can be linked to underlying neurobiological processes and translated into meaningful research outcomes. What can you expect from us? In accordance with the collective labor agreement for Dutch universities, we offer a salary of at least €                    3.204\n                    \n                    up to a maximum of €                    4.051                    (promovendus)\n                    gross per month for a full-time employment contract. 232 vacation hours per year, based on a 38-hour workweek (1.0 FTE). You can also work more or fewer hours in exchange for more or fewer free hours. For example, with a 40-hour workweek, you save 96 extra free hours, and with a 36-hour workweek, you lose 96 hours. End-of-year bonus of 8.3% and 8% holiday allowance. Extensive opportunities for personal and professional development. A fulltime position for the duration of 48 months. Where will you be working? At the University of Groningen (UG), researchers from all fields of academia and technology are working on academic challenges and societal questions. Lecturers prepare their students for meaningful careers within or outside the academic world. Interdisciplinary research and teaching, sharing of knowledge, collaboration with businesses, government institutions, and societal organizations are aspects that are of the utmost importance to this European top university. The UG aims to be an open academic community with an inclusive and safe working climate that invites you to add your value. The Faculty of Science and Engineering (FSE) provides teaching and research across a wide range of disciplines, from physics and biology to artificial intelligence, mechanical engineering, and pharmacy. In close collaboration with partners from industry, healthcare, and society, we contribute to the urgent challenges of our time, such as energy, sustainability, digitization, and medical technology. Our community is open and informal, with more than 7,000 students, 1,000 PhD students, and 1,400 staff members from all over the world. If you would like to learn more about the Faculty of Science and Engineering, visit rug.nl/fse . You will be embedded in an interdisciplinary research environment at the University of Groningen and work as part of the international consortium. Your research will involve collaboration with scientists working on longitudinal and multimodal datasets, clinical studies, biomarker development, evidence synthesis and stakeholder engagement. The position provides opportunities to: Work with longitudinal, multimodal and potentially multi-omics datasets. Develop and apply data-science methods to clinically relevant research questions. Contribute to systematic evidence synthesis and evidence mapping. Investigate relationships between digital proxies and neurobiological markers. Collaborate across disciplines and international research teams. Present your work at international conferences and publish in peer-reviewed journals; and Contribute to scientific outputs and activities across the project. You will also participate in the doctoral training and professional development activities offered by the University of Groningen and the relevant graduate school. This position is conditional upon the grant agreement being signed and the associated funding becoming available. string(27) \"sollicitatieprocedure_wp_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n  }\n} Application procedure Step 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Step 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Step 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Step 4: Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture. Step 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen! Interested? Does this vacancy appeal to you? If so, click on the button below and apply straightaway. Please add the following documents to your application: CV (incl. 2 references) Cover letter. Apply now Do you have any questions or need more information? Questions about the content of the job? Martien Kas Full Professor M.J.H.Kas@rug.nl Questions about your application process? Martien Kas Full Professor M.J.H.Kas@rug.nl Information about applying When scheduling meetings, we will take your schedule into account as much as possible. The University of Groningen considers social safety important. We strive to be a university where staff and students feel respected and at home, regardless of differences in background, experiences, perspectives, and identity. For more information, see also our page about our diversity policy . Acquisition is not appreciated. Our selection procedure follows the guidelines of the NVP Application Code. Read document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Go straight to All vacancies Working at UG Contact information University of Groningen PO Box 72 9700 AB Groningen The Netherlands How to find us Follow us on array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
    },
    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/phd-position-eeg-and-neurobiological-markers-2464/?lang=en": {
      "title": "PhD position EEG and Neurobiological Markers",
      "description": "PhD position EEG and Neurobiological Markers - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts PhD position EEG and Neurobiological Markers Apply now PhD PhD position EEG and Neurobiological Markers This vacancy is only available in English Are you a motivated early-career researcher with a strong interest in EEG, neurobiology, and precision medicine ? Would you like to investigate how neurobiological markers related to reward, motivation, and impulsivity can contribute to a better understanding of health and disease? We are looking for an enthusiastic PhD candidate to join an international, multidisciplinary research programme investigating reward, motivation, and impulsivity across major depressive disorder, Alzheimer’s disease, and obesity . Your PhD research will combine three closely connected components: a systematic review of EEG measures, empirical EEG analyses, and hypothesis-driven research investigating relationships between EEG and other neurobiological markers . The position provides an opportunity to develop expertise in EEG methodology and quantitative analysis while contributing to a broader precision medicine approach that integrates evidence across different populations, research settings, and types of biological and clinical data. Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 30 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time 1 FTE €3.204 - €4.051 Share this vacancy PhD position EEG and Neurobiological Markers Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/phd-position-eeg-and-neurobiological-markers-2464/?lang=en What are you going to do? Your PhD research will connect systematic evidence synthesis with empirical EEG research and hypothesis-driven investigation of neurobiological markers. Systematic review of EEG measures A first component of your research will be a systematic review of EEG measures relevant to reward, motivation, and impulsivity. You will: Develop and conduct a systematic review of EEG measures relevant to reward, motivation, and impulsivity. Define and document search strategies and eligibility criteria. Screen and select relevant scientific literature. Extract and organise information on EEG measures, study characteristics, populations, outcomes, and relevant neurobiological markers. Synthesise and map the available evidence in a transparent and reproducible manner. Investigate the consistency and potential relevance of different EEG measures across populations and research settings. Identify promising EEG measures as well as important gaps in the existing evidence. Contribute to scientific publications and other outputs arising from the evidence synthesis. This work will provide an evidence-based foundation for the interpretation and selection of EEG measures used in the empirical research. EEG analyses A substantial part of your PhD will involve analysing EEG data generated through cohort and clinical research. Depending on the available datasets and specific research questions, you will: Contribute to the preparation, preprocessing, and quality control of EEG data. Develop and apply appropriate EEG analysis pipelines. Investigate EEG measures relevant to reward, motivation, and impulsivity. Examine associations between EEG measures and behavioural, clinical, and other relevant variables. Analyse data collected across different populations and research settings. Contribute to the development of reproducible and well-documented analytical workflows. Interpret EEG findings in the context of the broader scientific framework. Communicate findings through scientific publications, presentations, and research meetings. You will progressively develop methodological independence and contribute to decisions concerning the analysis and interpretation of EEG data under the guidance of the supervisory team. Hypothesis testing with neurobiological markers A further aim of the PhD is to investigate hypothesis-driven relationships between EEG measures and other neurobiological markers . You will: Formulate and test hypotheses concerning relationships between neurobiological markers relevant to reward, motivation, and impulsivity. Investigate associations between EEG measures and other available biological, clinical, behavioural, or phenotypic measures. Examine whether neurobiological markers are associated with transdiagnostic dimensions of reward, motivation, and impulsivity or with relevant clinical outcomes. Apply appropriate statistical methods to test predefined hypotheses. Investigate whether combinations of neurobiological measures provide complementary information. Interpret findings in relation to existing evidence and the broader precision medicine framework. Contribute to understanding the potential of neurobiological markers for characterising clinically relevant profiles across different conditions. The precise analytical approaches will be developed in collaboration with the supervisory team and will depend on the available datasets and scientific questions. Integration of evidence and empirical research An important feature of the PhD is the connection between what is known from the literature and what can be learned from new data . You will therefore have the opportunity to: Use findings from the systematic review to inform empirical EEG analyses. Compare findings across different populations and research settings. Integrate EEG findings with other neurobiological, behavioural, and clinical measures. Critically evaluate the strengths and limitations of candidate biomarkers. Contribute to the identification of neurobiological measures that may have relevance across diagnostic categories. This integrated approach will allow you to develop a broad understanding of how EEG and other neurobiological measures can contribute to transdiagnostic and precision medicine research. Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 30 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time €3.204 - €4.051 Who are you? We are looking for a highly motivated candidate with a strong interest in neuroscience, EEG, and quantitative research . You have: A Master’s degree in neuroscience, biomedical sciences, psychology, cognitive science, medicine, biology, behavioural science, or a related discipline. A strong interest in human neurobiology and EEG research. Experience with quantitative research and statistical analysis. Experience with scientific literature and academic research. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. The ability to work systematically and accurately with scientific literature and complex datasets. Excellent written and spoken English. The ability to work independently while collaborating effectively within a multidisciplinary research team. A strong motivation to develop as an independent researcher and complete a PhD within four years. You do not need to be an expert in all EEG methodologies. We are particularly interested in candidates who have a strong scientific and quantitative foundation, some relevant experience with EEG or neurophysiological research, and the motivation to develop further methodological expertise during the PhD. It is an advantage if you have Practical experience with EEG data collection, preprocessing, analysis, or interpretation. Familiarity with EEG-derived measures, such as event-related potentials, spectral measures, or time-frequency measures. Experience with EEG analysis software or programming environments such as MATLAB, Python, or R. Experience with statistical modelling or other quantitative analytical approaches. Experience working with clinical, cohort, or population-based datasets. Experience with multimodal or longitudinal data. Experience conducting systematic or scoping reviews. Familiarity with systematic-review methodology, literature searching, screening, and data extraction. Experience with biological or neurobiological markers. Knowledge of reward, motivation, impulsivity, or related cognitive and affective processes. Experience with open and reproducible research practices. Experience in all of these areas is not required. We value scientific curiosity, methodological foundations, analytical thinking, and the ability and motivation to learn new methods . What can you expect from us? In accordance with the collective labor agreement for Dutch universities, we offer a salary of at least €                    3.204\n                    \n                    up to a maximum of €                    4.051                    (promovendus)\n                    gross per month for a full-time employment contract. 232 vacation hours per year, based on a 38-hour workweek (1.0 FTE). You can also work more or fewer hours in exchange for more or fewer free hours. For example, with a 40-hour workweek, you save 96 extra free hours, and with a 36-hour workweek, you lose 96 hours. End-of-year bonus of 8.3% and 8% holiday allowance. Extensive opportunities for personal and professional development. Temporary appointment for 1.0 FTE for 4 years. Where will you be working? At the University of Groningen (UG), researchers from all fields of academia and technology are working on academic challenges and societal questions. Lecturers prepare their students for meaningful careers within or outside the academic world. Interdisciplinary research and teaching, sharing of knowledge, collaboration with businesses, government institutions, and societal organizations are aspects that are of the utmost importance to this European top university. The UG aims to be an open academic community with an inclusive and safe working climate that invites you to add your value. The Faculty of Science and Engineering (FSE) provides teaching and research across a wide range of disciplines, from physics and biology to artificial intelligence, mechanical engineering, and pharmacy. In close collaboration with partners from industry, healthcare, and society, we contribute to the urgent challenges of our time, such as energy, sustainability, digitization, and medical technology. Our community is open and informal, with more than 7,000 students, 1,000 PhD students, and 1,400 staff members from all over the world. If you would like to learn more about the Faculty of Science and Engineering, visit rug.nl/fse . You will be based at the University of Groningen and become part of the GELIFES institute Neurobiology expertise group. You will work within an interdisciplinary research environment bringing together expertise in neuroscience, evidence synthesis, data analysis, and precision medicine. The research involves collaboration with academic and clinical researchers and other partners in an international research consortium. About the research programme The research programme aims to develop a transdiagnostic precision medicine framework for reward, motivation, and impulsivity across major depressive disorder, Alzheimer’s disease, and obesity. The programme combines cohort research, clinical studies, biomarker research, systematic evidence synthesis, and stakeholder engagement. It seeks to identify and evaluate measures that can improve the understanding and characterisation of reward, motivation, and impulsivity across different conditions. Your PhD will contribute specifically to the investigation of EEG and other neurobiological markers . By combining systematic evidence synthesis with empirical EEG analyses and hypothesis-driven research, you will contribute to understanding the potential value of neurobiological measures within a transdiagnostic precision medicine framework. This position is conditional upon the grant agreement being signed and the associated funding becoming available. string(27) \"sollicitatieprocedure_wp_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n  }\n} Application procedure Step 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Step 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Step 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Step 4: Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture. Step 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen! Interested? Does this vacancy appeal to you? If so, click on the button below and apply straightaway. Please add the following documents to your application: CV Cover letter (incl. name of two references). Apply now Do you have any questions or need more information? Questions about the content of the job? Martien Kas Full Professor M.J.H.Kas@rug.nl Questions about your application process? Martien Kas Full Professor M.J.H.Kas@rug.nl Information about applying When scheduling meetings, we will take your schedule into account as much as possible. The University of Groningen considers social safety important. We strive to be a university where staff and students feel respected and at home, regardless of differences in background, experiences, perspectives, and identity. For more information, see also our page about our diversity policy . Acquisition is not appreciated. Our selection procedure follows the guidelines of the NVP Application Code. Read document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Go straight to All vacancies Working at UG Contact information University of Groningen PO Box 72 9700 AB Groningen The Netherlands How to find us Follow us on array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
    },
    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/bestuurder-faculteit-science-engineering-2402/?lang=en": {
      "title": "Bestuurder Faculteit Science & Engineering",
      "description": "Bestuurder Faculteit Science & Engineering - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts Bestuurder Faculteit Science & Engineering Apply now Bestuurder Faculteit Science & Engineering This vacancy is only available in Dutch Wil jij als bestuurder impact maken op de koers en ontwikkeling van de Faculty of Science and Engineering (FSE)? Weet jij ambities op het gebied van onderwijs en onderzoek te verbinden aan strategische keuzes rondom personeel, financiën, huisvesting en organisatie? Dan zoeken wij jou als bestuurder. Als lid van het faculteitsbestuur geef je samen met de decaan en vicedecaan richting aan de toekomst van FSE. Vanuit jouw brede portefeuille zorg je ervoor dat ambities worden vertaald naar een toekomstbestendige en doelmatige organisatie. Juist in een periode waarin financiële uitdagingen om scherpe keuzes vragen, krijg je de ruimte én verantwoordelijkheid om verschil te maken. Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 12 oktober 2026 0.8 - 1 FTE €8.309 - €10.815 Share this vacancy Bestuurder Faculteit Science & Engineering Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/bestuurder-faculteit-science-engineering-2402/?lang=en Wat ga je doen? Het faculteitsbestuur bestaat uit drie leden. Deze werken samen als een team en opereren als een collegiaal bestuur. Zij hebben ieder eigen aandachtsgebieden. De decaan fungeert als voorzitter en bewaakt het functioneren van het bestuur. Het faculteitsbestuur wordt bijgestaan door een student-assessor en ondersteund door een beleidsdirecteur en secretaris. Als bestuurder ben je verantwoordelijk voor personeel, financiën, huisvesting, beheer van de gebouwen en alle andere zaken op het gebied van de bedrijfsvoering. Samen met de decaan en de vicedecaan, met respectievelijk de portefeuilles onderzoek/algemene zaken en onderwijs, draag je de eindverantwoordelijkheid voor de facultaire beleidsontwikkeling en–uitvoering. Je draagt zorg voor de doelmatige organisatie van de faculteit en geeft leiding aan de (hoofden) van facultaire diensten. Daarnaast heb je een rol – samen met collega’s van andere faculteiten- bij de totstandkoming en uitvoering van het instellingsbeleid voor bedrijfsvoering. De functie vereist in het bijzonder dat je: • Het onderzoeks- en onderwijsbeleid vertaalt naar het beslag op alle soorten van middelen, in het bijzonder de personele en financiële middelen en de huisvesting. • Dit beleid eveneens vertaalt naar de vereiste vormen en omvang van ondersteuning aan de wetenschappelijke staf en naar een doelmatige inrichting van de facultaire organisatie. Dit alles moet worden vormgegeven in uitdagende financiële omstandigheden. Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 12 oktober 2026 €8.309 - €10.815 Wie ben jij? Je bent een enthousiaste, gedreven professional: Met een academisch werk- en denkniveau en een sterk ontwikkeld strategisch denkvermogen. Met managementervaring bij een (grote) publieke instelling in het (hoger)onderwijs en affiniteit met wetenschappelijk onderwijs en onderzoek. Met ervaring met de financiële controlcyclus, bestuurlijke processen en administratieve procedures. Je bent helder en duidelijk over de procedures en toont souplesse waar nodig. Met ervaring op het gebied van talent- en organisatieontwikkeling, veranderingsprocessen, arbeidsvoorwaarden en andere HR-onderwerpen. Met een goed gevoel voor bestuurlijke verhoudingen en je bent daardoor in staat om met gezag te werken in een omgeving waarin professionele autonomie een grote rol speelt. Je kunt goed relaties leggen en onderhouden. Met een coachende stijl van leidinggeven en het vermogen tot delegeren waar dat mogelijk is. Met goede communicatieve vaardigheden, zowel in woord als in geschrift, in de Nederlandse en de Engelse taal. Die betrouwbaar is in afspraken en uitspraken. Die het prettig vindt om snel te schakelen tussen de vele bestuurlijke zaken, die goed past in de cultuur van de faculteit en die ook het organisatiebelang van de gehele RUG dient. Wat kan je van ons verwachten? Wij bieden, in overeenstemming met cao Nederlandse Universiteiten een salaris van minimaal €                    8.309\n                    \n                    tot maximaal €                    10.815                    (salary scale 16)\n                    bruto per maand bij een fulltime dienstverband. 232 verlofuren per jaar, o.b.v. een 38-urige werkweek (1.0 fte). Je kunt ook meer of minder uren werken, in ruil voor meer of minder vrije uren. Zo spaar je bij een 40-urige werkweek 96 extra vrije uren en lever je bij een 36-urige werkweek 96 uur in. Eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3% en 8% vakantietoeslag. Uitgebreide mogelijkheden voor persoonlijke en professionele ontwikkeling. Aanstelling zal plaatsvinden voor een periode van één jaar met uitzicht op een dienstverband voor onbepaalde tijd bij gebleken geschiktheid. De benoeming tot bestuurder is in principe voor vijf jaar met de mogelijkheid tot verlenging met vijf jaar. Waar ga je werken? Bij de Rijksuniversiteit Groningen (RUG) werk je bij een brede topuniversiteit, met aandacht voor alle takken van wetenschap en techniek. Ondersteunende medewerkers leveren een essentiële bijdrage aan de inzet van docenten en onderzoekers voor de ontwikkeling van talent en een betere, duurzame samenleving. De RUG wil een open academische gemeenschap zijn met een inclusief en veilig werkklimaat dat je uitnodigt om jouw waarde toe te voegen. The Faculty of Science and Engineering (FSE) provides teaching and research across a wide range of disciplines, from physics and biology to artificial intelligence, mechanical engineering, and pharmacy. In close collaboration with partners from industry, healthcare, and society, we contribute to the urgent challenges of our time, such as energy, sustainability, digitization, and medical technology. Our community is open and informal, with more than 7,000 students, 1,000 PhD students, and 1,400 staff members from all over the world. If you would like to learn more about the Faculty of Science and Engineering, visit rug.nl/fse . De missie van de Faculty of Science and Engineering richt zich op de drie pijlers onderzoek, onderwijs, en maatschappelijke impact, binnen een breed scala van de bèta- en techniekwetenschappen, en in samenwerking met partners binnen en buiten de Universiteit. Onze onderzoekers dragen bij aan het ontwikkelen van fundamentele kennis en aan het vinden van innovatieve oplossingen voor wereldwijde problemen waarmee de maatschappij te maken krijgt op het gebied van gezondheid, energie, digitalisering, duurzaamheid en weerbaarheid. Onze facultaire gemeenschap heeft een open, informeel karakter, met medewerkers en studenten uit de hele wereld. De faculteit is momenteel bezig met het formuleren van de strategie voor 2026-2031, aansluitend bij en voortbouwend op de strategie van de Universiteit. string(24) \"sollicitatieprocedure_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(69) \"Second interview and possible assessment and/or requesting references\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(145) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. This interview can be complemented with an assessment. We may also ask for references at this point.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(455) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\r\n\r\nCurious about what the onboarding process at the University of Groningen looks like? On our information page for new employees , you can read what to expect.\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(69) \"Second interview and possible assessment and/or requesting references\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(145) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. This interview can be complemented with an assessment. We may also ask for references at this point.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(455) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\r\n\r\nCurious about what the onboarding process at the University of Groningen looks like? On our information page for new employees , you can read what to expect.\"\n  }\n} Sollicitatieprocedure Stap 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Stap 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Stap 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Stap 4: Second interview and possible assessment and/or requesting references We may schedule a second interview with you. This interview can be complemented with an assessment. We may also ask for references at this point. Stap 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\r\n\r\nCurious about what the onboarding process at the University of Groningen looks like? On our information page for new employees , you can read what to expect. Interesse? Klinkt dit als een uitdaging die bij je past? Solliciteer dan direct via onderstaande knop! Voeg bij je sollicitatie de volgende documenten toe: CV. Motivatiebrief. Solliciteer nu Heb je vragen of meer informatie nodig? Heb je vragen over de inhoud van de vacature? Rob Timmermans Hoogleraar R.G.E.Timmermans@rug.nl Heb je vragen over de sollicitatieprocedure? Grytsje van der Meer Beleidsmedewerker Grytsje.van.der.Meer@rug.nl Informatie over solliciteren Bij de planning van de gesprekken houden wij zoveel mogelijk rekening met jouw agenda. De Rijksuniversiteit Groningen vindt sociale veiligheid belangrijk. We streven ernaar een universiteit te zijn waar medewerkers en studenten zich gerespecteerd en thuis voelen, ongeacht verschillen in achtergronden, ervaringen, perspectieven en identiteit. Voor meer informatie zie ook onze pagina over ons diversiteitsbeleid . Acquisitie wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Onze selectieprocedure volgt de richtlijnen van de NVP Sollicitatiecode Lees hier het document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Jump to Alle vacatures Werken bij RUG Contactinformatie Rijksuniversiteit Groningen Postbus 72 9700 AB Groningen Waar vindt u ons Volg ons op array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
    },
    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/phd-position-on-materials-development-for-electrically-driven-water-treatment-processes-2486/?lang=en": {
      "title": "PhD position on materials development for electrically-driven water treatment processes",
      "description": "PhD position on materials development for electrically-driven water treatment processes - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts PhD position on materials development for electrically-driven water treatment processes Apply now PhD PhD position on materials development for electrically-driven water treatment processes This vacancy is only available in English In the Engineering and Technology Institute Groningen (ENTEG), we are looking for a talented and motivated PhD student for the development and evaluation of advanced electrode materials and cell component development for sustainable electrochemical water purification technologies. Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 30 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time 1 FTE €3.204 - €4.051 Share this vacancy PhD position on materials development for electrically-driven water treatment processes Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/phd-position-on-materials-development-for-electrically-driven-water-treatment-processes-2486/?lang=en What are you going to do? In many industrial processes, chemicals are added to treat water, clean installations or separate substances from each other. Before the water can be reused or discharged, those excipients must be removed again. That costs a lot of energy, chemicals and money. The new project ECO (Electrically-driven, Chemical-free Operations) therefore chooses a different approach: prevent those excipients from being needed at all. The project will use electric fields and local pH changes close to electrodes to create the desired conditions in exactly the right place without adjusting the entire liquid. Within ECO, the PhD candidate will collaborate with 4 other PhD researchers from the University of Twente TU Delft, Wageningen University & Research and the University of Copenhagen. Companies such as Royal Avebe, FrieslandCampina, Nobian, Shell, ISPT, Ecolab and VNP are also involved in the consortium. With five PhD candidates, the consortium will investigate in the coming years how electrically driven process technologies can contribute to cleaner and more energy-efficient industrial processes. Responsibilities and tasks: Fabrication of materials and electrochemical cells with targeted characteristics. Characterization of materials and relevant interfaces for their role in the reaction mechanisms. Preparation of scientific articles and conference communications. Teaching activities (10% of total workload), including assistance to courses, as well as supervision of Bachelor and Master students. Contribution to the scientific and collaborative research environment in Chemical Engineering group and the ENTEG institute. A team player and open to collaborating in a consortium of other researchers and industrial partners, with regular consortium meetings. Ability to communicate their research to people with a broad, technical background. Handling the ‘uncertainty’ that the details of the project still need to be defined. Contribution to defining their own research, in concerted agreement with the consortium. Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 30 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time €3.204 - €4.051 Who are you? A Master’s degree (or an equivalent university degree) in Chemical Engineering, Materials Science, Chemistry, or related discipline. We are looking for a talented, motivated and enthusiastic researcher. Analytical skills, initiative and creativity are highly desired. You are a naturally curious person who is eager to learn more and has a strong interest in research. Excellent written and oral communication skills in English are a prerequisite. We prefer candidates with a good team spirit, who like to work in an internationally oriented, social environment. What can you expect from us? In accordance with the collective labor agreement for Dutch universities, we offer a salary of at least €                    3.204\n                    \n                    up to a maximum of €                    4.051                    (promovendus)\n                    gross per month for a full-time employment contract. 232 vacation hours per year, based on a 38-hour workweek (1.0 FTE). You can also work more or fewer hours in exchange for more or fewer free hours. For example, with a 40-hour workweek, you save 96 extra free hours, and with a 36-hour workweek, you lose 96 hours. End-of-year bonus of 8.3% and 8% holiday allowance. Extensive opportunities for personal and professional development. First, you will get a temporary position of one year with the option of renewal for another three years; prolongation of the contract is contingent on sufficient progress in the first year to indicate that successful completion of the PhD thesis within the contract period is to be expected. A PhD training program is part of the agreement and you will be enrolled in the Graduate School of the Faculty of Science and Engineering. Where will you be working? At the University of Groningen (UG), researchers from all fields of academia and technology are working on academic challenges and societal questions. Lecturers prepare their students for meaningful careers within or outside the academic world. Interdisciplinary research and teaching, sharing of knowledge, collaboration with businesses, government institutions, and societal organizations are aspects that are of the utmost importance to this European top university. The UG aims to be an open academic community with an inclusive and safe working climate that invites you to add your value. The Faculty of Science and Engineering (FSE) provides teaching and research across a wide range of disciplines, from physics and biology to artificial intelligence, mechanical engineering, and pharmacy. In close collaboration with partners from industry, healthcare, and society, we contribute to the urgent challenges of our time, such as energy, sustainability, digitization, and medical technology. Our community is open and informal, with more than 7,000 students, 1,000 PhD students, and 1,400 staff members from all over the world. If you would like to learn more about the Faculty of Science and Engineering, visit rug.nl/fse . The Engineering and Technology institute Groningen (ENTEG) in which this position is embedded is the engineering science and technology institute of the University of Groningen, The Netherlands. ENTEG research is highly multidisciplinary in nature and focuses on fundamental and applied research on the development of new and innovative processes and products for a wide range of product sectors. Process driven research activities are performed in the field of chemical and biochemical systems, mechanical and electric systems and system networks. Typical product sectors include biobased products, tailored, complex materials such as advanced polymers or polymeric formulations, catalysts, mechatronic devices and software and algorithms. Design, control and modelling and analyses complement the activities. string(27) \"sollicitatieprocedure_wp_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n  }\n} Application procedure Step 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Step 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Step 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Step 4: Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture. Step 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen! Interested? Does this vacancy appeal to you? If so, click on the button below and apply straightaway. Please add the following documents to your application: Cover letter. Curriculum vitae. Transcripts from your Bachelor’s and Master’s degree. Any other relevant documents (e.g., short research statement, awards, publications, language skills/certification, references). Apply now Do you have any questions or need more information? Questions about the content of the job? Vassilis Kyriakou Associate Professor v.kyriakou@rug.nl Questions about your application process? Kimberley ter Voorde - Speelman Human Resources Assistant k.m.ter.voorde-speelman@rug.nl Information about applying When scheduling meetings, we will take your schedule into account as much as possible. The University of Groningen considers social safety important. We strive to be a university where staff and students feel respected and at home, regardless of differences in background, experiences, perspectives, and identity. For more information, see also our page about our diversity policy . Acquisition is not appreciated. Our selection procedure follows the guidelines of the NVP Application Code. Read document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Go straight to All vacancies Working at UG Contact information University of Groningen PO Box 72 9700 AB Groningen The Netherlands How to find us Follow us on array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
    },
    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/phd-position-on-electrochemical-synthesis-of-ammonia-in-ceramic-membrane-reactors-2485/?lang=en": {
      "title": "PhD position on electrochemical synthesis of ammonia in ceramic membrane reactors",
      "description": "PhD position on electrochemical synthesis of ammonia in ceramic membrane reactors - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts PhD position on electrochemical synthesis of ammonia in ceramic membrane reactors Apply now PhD PhD position on electrochemical synthesis of ammonia in ceramic membrane reactors This vacancy is only available in English In the Engineering and Technology Institute Groningen (ENTEG), we are looking for a talented and motivated PhD student for the development and evaluation of (electro)catalysts for electrochemical ammonia synthesis from sustainable sources in ceramic electrochemical reactors. Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 30 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time 1 FTE €3.204 - €4.051 Share this vacancy PhD position on electrochemical synthesis of ammonia in ceramic membrane reactors Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/phd-position-on-electrochemical-synthesis-of-ammonia-in-ceramic-membrane-reactors-2485/?lang=en What are you going to do? Ammonia is not only a key-chemical for sustaining global population, but also an intriguing carbon-free energy carrier. Ammonia, however, is the most energy intensive commodity chemical, responsible for 1-2% of energy consumption and CO2 emissions worldwide. The PhD project will support the efforts for creating innovative electrochemical membrane reactors that produce sustainable ammonia at high efficiency for decentralized applications. The PhD research will be part of the 20.3 Meuros HyNITROGEN project (https://groenvermogennl.org/rd/werkpakket-5/) of the National Growthfund GroenvermogenNL. This unique consortium brings together more than 40 companies, universities and research institutes, covering the entire value chain. Responsibilities and tasks: Synthesis and characterization of electrocatalysts at intermediate and high temperatures. Fabrication of single cells with targeted characteristics. Characterization of materials and relevant interfaces for their role in the reaction mechanisms. Preparation of scientific articles and conference communications. Teaching activities (10% of total workload), including assistance to courses, as well as supervision of Bachelor and Master students. Contribution to the scientific and collaborative research environment in Chemical Engineering group and the ENTEG institute. Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 30 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time €3.204 - €4.051 Who are you? A Master’s degree (or an equivalent university degree) in Chemical Engineering, Materials Science, Chemistry, or related discipline. We are looking for a talented, motivated and enthusiastic researcher. Analytical skills, initiative and creativity are highly desired. You are a naturally curious person who is eager to learn more and has a strong interest in research. Excellent written and oral communication skills in English are a prerequisite. We prefer candidates with a good team spirit, who like to work in an internationally oriented, social environment. What can you expect from us? In accordance with the collective labor agreement for Dutch universities, we offer a salary of at least €                    3.204\n                    \n                    up to a maximum of €                    4.051                    (promovendus)\n                    gross per month for a full-time employment contract. 232 vacation hours per year, based on a 38-hour workweek (1.0 FTE). You can also work more or fewer hours in exchange for more or fewer free hours. For example, with a 40-hour workweek, you save 96 extra free hours, and with a 36-hour workweek, you lose 96 hours. End-of-year bonus of 8.3% and 8% holiday allowance. Extensive opportunities for personal and professional development. First, you will get a temporary position of one year with the option of renewal for another three years; prolongation of the contract is contingent on sufficient progress in the first year to indicate that successful completion of the PhD thesis within the contract period is to be expected. A PhD training program is part of the agreement and you will be enrolled in the Graduate School of the Faculty of Science and Engineering. Where will you be working? At the University of Groningen (UG), researchers from all fields of academia and technology are working on academic challenges and societal questions. Lecturers prepare their students for meaningful careers within or outside the academic world. Interdisciplinary research and teaching, sharing of knowledge, collaboration with businesses, government institutions, and societal organizations are aspects that are of the utmost importance to this European top university. The UG aims to be an open academic community with an inclusive and safe working climate that invites you to add your value. The Faculty of Science and Engineering (FSE) provides teaching and research across a wide range of disciplines, from physics and biology to artificial intelligence, mechanical engineering, and pharmacy. In close collaboration with partners from industry, healthcare, and society, we contribute to the urgent challenges of our time, such as energy, sustainability, digitization, and medical technology. Our community is open and informal, with more than 7,000 students, 1,000 PhD students, and 1,400 staff members from all over the world. If you would like to learn more about the Faculty of Science and Engineering, visit rug.nl/fse . The Engineering and Technology institute Groningen (ENTEG) in which this position is embedded is the engineering science and technology institute of the University of Groningen, The Netherlands. ENTEG research is highly multidisciplinary in nature and focuses on fundamental and applied research on the development of new and innovative processes and products for a wide range of product sectors. Process driven research activities are performed in the field of chemical and biochemical systems, mechanical and electric systems and system networks. Typical product sectors include biobased products, tailored, complex materials such as advanced polymers or polymeric formulations, catalysts, mechatronic devices and software and algorithms. Design, control and modelling and analyses complement the activities. string(27) \"sollicitatieprocedure_wp_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n  }\n} Application procedure Step 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Step 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Step 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Step 4: Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture. Step 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen! Interested? Does this vacancy appeal to you? If so, click on the button below and apply straightaway. Please add the following documents to your application: Cover letter. Curriculum vitae. Transcripts from your Bachelor’s and Master’s degree. Any other relevant documents (e.g., short research statement, awards, publications, language skills/certification, references). An interview, a scientific presentation and a writing assignment are part of the selection procedure. Apply now Do you have any questions or need more information? Questions about the content of the job? Vassilis Kyriakou Associate Professor v.kyriakou@rug.nl Questions about your application process? Kimberley ter Voorde - Speelman Human Resources Assistant k.m.ter.voorde-speelman@rug.nl Information about applying When scheduling meetings, we will take your schedule into account as much as possible. The University of Groningen considers social safety important. We strive to be a university where staff and students feel respected and at home, regardless of differences in background, experiences, perspectives, and identity. For more information, see also our page about our diversity policy . Acquisition is not appreciated. Our selection procedure follows the guidelines of the NVP Application Code. Read document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Go straight to All vacancies Working at UG Contact information University of Groningen PO Box 72 9700 AB Groningen The Netherlands How to find us Follow us on array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
    },
    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/programmamanager-sustainable-energy-conversion-2421/?lang=en": {
      "title": "Programmamanager sustainable energy conversion",
      "description": "Programmamanager sustainable energy conversion - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts Programmamanager sustainable energy conversion Apply now Programmamanager sustainable energy conversion This vacancy is only available in Dutch Wil jij meewerken aan de energiesystemen van de toekomst? Krijg je energie van het verbinden van onderzoek, onderwijs en innovatie? Als programmamanager bij het Energy and Sustainability Research Institute Groningen (ESRIG) werk je binnen de faculteit Science and Engineering aan toonaangevende projecten op het gebied van geïntegreerde energiesystemen en de waterstofwaardeketen. Samen met onderzoekers, onderwijsprofessionals en regionale partners draag je bij aan de verdere ontwikkeling van de waterstofregio Noord-Nederland. Dan zijn wij bij het Energie- en Duurzaamheid Onderzoeksinstituut Groningen op zoek naar jou! Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 18 oktober 2026 0.8 - 1 FTE €4.925 - €6.682 Share this vacancy Programmamanager sustainable energy conversion Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/programmamanager-sustainable-energy-conversion-2421/?lang=en Wat ga je doen? Als programmamanager speel je een sleutelrol in verschillende cruciale projecten binnen de waterstof vallei Noord-Nederland. Je werkt onder andere aan de GroenvermogenNL-projecten HyLEARN en HyUSE, maar ook aan diverse regionale programma’s voor leven lang ontwikkelen (LLO) op het gebied van waterstoftoepassingen en groene moleculen.. Je belangrijkste project is HyLEARN ( https://groenvermogennl.org/en/nieuws/drie-regionale-projecten-van-start-met-ontwikkeling-van-learning-communities-binnen-de-waterstofketen/ ) . In dit project komen technologie en talentontwikkeling samen. HyLEARN onderzoekt hoe technische en digitale innovaties de ‘time-to-job’ kunnen verkorten. Dit is de tijd tussen het ontstaan van een behoefte aan bepaalde vaardigheden en het moment waarop voldoende professionals daarover beschikken. Als programmamanager verbind je onderzoek, ontwikkeling en onderwijs, en heb je de volgende verantwoordelijkheden Het coördineren van de resultaten en activiteiten binnen HyLEARN, samen met de projectcoördinator en de technisch manager. Het ontwikkelen en versterken van de actieve leergemeenschappen op het gebied van waterstof. Het coördineren van activiteiten rond de toegang tot regionale laboratoria. Het initiëren en organiseren van brainstormsessies waarin nieuwe ideeën en samenwerkingen ontstaan. Het vertegenwoordigen van de Rijksuniversiteit Groningen bij bijvoorbeeld projectvergaderingen, conferenties en projectontwikkeling. Het aansturen van onderzoek naar: numerieke modellering van elektrochemische processen in energiesystemen. realtime simulaties van geïntegreerde energiesystemen. schaalmodel testen van elektrochemische conversietechnologie. pedagogische methoden voor dynamische curricula. Je beweegt daarbij voortdurend tussen inhoud, mensen en organisaties. Daarmee lever je niet alleen een bijdrage aan succesvolle onderzoeks- en onderwijsprojecten, maar ook aan de ontwikkeling van de kennis en vaardigheden die nodig zijn voor de energietransitie. Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 18 oktober 2026 €4.925 - €6.682 Wie ben jij? Voor deze programmamanager-rol zoeken we iemand die beschikt over de volgende kwalificaties/ eigenschappen Een afgeronde masteropleiding (of gelijkwaardig niveau) in natuurwetenschappen, techniek of onderwijskunde. 3 tot 5 jaar relevante werkervaring in een projectgerichte organisatie. Aantoonbare ervaring met onderzoek en ontwikkeling op het gebied van energie(omzettings)systemen, waterstoftoepassingen, elektro(chemische) laboratoria of industriële processen. Sterk overtuigingsvermogen en het vermogen om de belangen van belanghebbenden zowel binnen een academische omgeving als in het ‘Hydrogen Valley’-ecosysteem tegen elkaar af te wegen. Sterke communicatieve vaardigheden in het Nederlands en Engels In het bezit zijn van jouw VCA is een pré. Daarnaast zoeken we iemand die Goed omgaat met complexiteit: je weet je weg te vinden in projecten waarin planning en resultaten niet altijd vooraf vaststaan. Je houdt overzicht, kunt omgaan met onzekerheid en weet verschillende, soms overlappende activiteiten effectief met elkaar te verbinden. Innovatie weet om te zetten in kansen: je ziet mogelijkheden om academische innovaties verder te brengen en te verbinden aan onderzoeks- en onderwijsinitiatieven binnen de Rijksuniversiteit Groningen. Daarbij werk je samen met partners binnen het R&D-ecosysteem om nieuwe projecten en initiatieven te ontwikkelen. Makkelijk verbinding maakt: je bouwt en onderhoudt goede werkrelaties, werkt graag samen met verschillende collega’s en partners en draagt actief bij aan een inclusieve werkomgeving. Wat kan je van ons verwachten? Wij bieden, in overeenstemming met cao Nederlandse Universiteiten een salaris van minimaal €                    4.925\n                    \n                    tot maximaal €                    6.682                    (schaal 11)\n                    bruto per maand bij een fulltime dienstverband. 232 verlofuren per jaar, o.b.v. een 38-urige werkweek (1.0 fte). Je kunt ook meer of minder uren werken, in ruil voor meer of minder vrije uren. Zo spaar je bij een 40-urige werkweek 96 extra vrije uren en lever je bij een 36-urige werkweek 96 uur in. Eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3% en 8% vakantietoeslag. Uitgebreide mogelijkheden voor persoonlijke en professionele ontwikkeling. Dit is een aanstelling dat wordt gefinancieerd vanuit het HyLEARN project. De duur van de aanstelling is 12 maanden en na deze periode is een eventuele verlenging van nogmaals 12 maanden mogelijk. Waar ga je werken? Bij de Rijksuniversiteit Groningen (RUG) werk je bij een brede topuniversiteit, met aandacht voor alle takken van wetenschap en techniek. Ondersteunende medewerkers leveren een essentiële bijdrage aan de inzet van docenten en onderzoekers voor de ontwikkeling van talent en een betere, duurzame samenleving. De RUG wil een open academische gemeenschap zijn met een inclusief en veilig werkklimaat dat je uitnodigt om jouw waarde toe te voegen. The Faculty of Science and Engineering (FSE) provides teaching and research across a wide range of disciplines, from physics and biology to artificial intelligence, mechanical engineering, and pharmacy. In close collaboration with partners from industry, healthcare, and society, we contribute to the urgent challenges of our time, such as energy, sustainability, digitization, and medical technology. Our community is open and informal, with more than 7,000 students, 1,000 PhD students, and 1,400 staff members from all over the world. If you would like to learn more about the Faculty of Science and Engineering, visit rug.nl/fse . Binnen dit regionale project werk je samen met een breed scala aan partners en collega’s, zoals regionale energiebedrijven, onderwijsinstellingen op MBO- en HBO-niveau, postdocs en projectcoördinatoren. Daarnaast val je onder de vakgroep Energy Conversion, die bestaat uit een15 onderzoekers en docenten. Het ESRIG (Energy and Sustainability Research Institute Groningen) telt in totaal 120 mensen, wat zorgt voor een dynamische en multidisciplinaire omgeving. Kortom: je werkt in een omgeving waar onderwijs, onderzoek en de praktijk van energie en duurzaamheid samenkomen, met veel ruimte voor kennisuitwisseling en innovatie! string(24) \"sollicitatieprocedure_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(69) \"Second interview and possible assessment and/or requesting references\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(145) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. This interview can be complemented with an assessment. We may also ask for references at this point.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(455) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\n\nCurious about what the onboarding process at the University of Groningen looks like? On our information page for new employees , you can read what to expect.\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(69) \"Second interview and possible assessment and/or requesting references\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(145) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. This interview can be complemented with an assessment. We may also ask for references at this point.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(455) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\n\nCurious about what the onboarding process at the University of Groningen looks like? On our information page for new employees , you can read what to expect.\"\n  }\n} Sollicitatieprocedure Stap 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Stap 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Stap 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Stap 4: Second interview and possible assessment and/or requesting references We may schedule a second interview with you. This interview can be complemented with an assessment. We may also ask for references at this point. Stap 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\n\nCurious about what the onboarding process at the University of Groningen looks like? On our information page for new employees , you can read what to expect. Interesse? Klinkt dit als een uitdaging die bij je past? Solliciteer dan direct via onderstaande knop! Voeg bij je sollicitatie de volgende documenten toe: CV. Motivatiebrief. Solliciteer nu Heb je vragen of meer informatie nodig? Heb je vragen over de inhoud van de vacature? Arjen van der Meer Universitair docent a.a.van.der.meer@rug.nl Heb je vragen over de sollicitatieprocedure? Dorien Smit HR-adviseur dorien.smit@rug.nl Informatie over solliciteren Bij de planning van de gesprekken houden wij zoveel mogelijk rekening met jouw agenda. De Rijksuniversiteit Groningen vindt sociale veiligheid belangrijk. We streven ernaar een universiteit te zijn waar medewerkers en studenten zich gerespecteerd en thuis voelen, ongeacht verschillen in achtergronden, ervaringen, perspectieven en identiteit. Voor meer informatie zie ook onze pagina over ons diversiteitsbeleid . Acquisitie wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Onze selectieprocedure volgt de richtlijnen van de NVP Sollicitatiecode Lees hier het document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Jump to Alle vacatures Werken bij RUG Contactinformatie Rijksuniversiteit Groningen Postbus 72 9700 AB Groningen Waar vindt u ons Volg ons op array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
    },
    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/postdoc-spatial-dynamics-and-interactions-of-terrestrial-and-aerial-predators-of-ground-breeding-birds-2456/?lang=en": {
      "title": "Postdoc Spatial dynamics and interactions of terrestrial and aerial predators of ground-breeding birds",
      "description": "Postdoc Spatial dynamics and interactions of terrestrial and aerial predators of ground-breeding birds - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts Postdoc Spatial dynamics and interactions of terrestrial and aerial predators of ground-breeding birds Apply now Post-doc Researcher Postdoc Spatial dynamics and interactions of terrestrial and aerial predators of ground-breeding birds This vacancy is only available in English We have a postdoc position open for the period of 3 years (0.8 FTE) within the PREDWEI 2 project. The aim of the project is to improve understanding of the spatial dynamics and shifting interactions among different predator species—both terrestrial and aerial—affecting ground-breeding birds (meadow, arable, and coastal species). The project will produce recommendations for effective management and policy regarding the various predator species, with the aim of increasing chick survival. The research will make an important contribution to knowledge on effective management for the conservation of ground-breeding birds and will identify the remaining knowledge gaps after completion of the study. Previous PREDWEI studies have provided substantial insight into the important role of various terrestrial predator species and their interactions in relation to ground-breeding birds. At the same time, these studies have revealed important knowledge gaps that are highly relevant for improving the effectiveness of policy and management aimed at protecting ground-breeding birds. This applies to the main landscape types in which these birds occur: meadow, arable, and coastal habitats, each with its own community of terrestrial and aerial predators (mammals and birds of prey). In each landscape type, a link will be established between nest and chick survival of ground-breeding birds and the occurrence, spatial habitat use, and diet of the various predators. This will be achieved through continued monitoring (predators, nests, and voles), diet studies (eDNA analyses of faeces and/or prey remains), and the expansion of telemetry studies of birds of prey. In this way, PREDWEI 2 builds on previous PREDWEI subprojects, while expanding the research to include the role of birds of prey through tracking studies. PREDWEI 2 will actively collaborate with several partner projects, including the Godwit Chick Survival Project, two arable bird pilot projects, and the Wij en Wadvogels project. The project will also make use of data obtained from various smaller and often fragmented predation studies across the Netherlands. Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 19 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time 0.8 FTE €4.251 - €4.422 Share this vacancy Postdoc Spatial dynamics and interactions of terrestrial and aerial predators of ground-breeding birds Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/postdoc-spatial-dynamics-and-interactions-of-terrestrial-and-aerial-predators-of-ground-breeding-birds-2456/?lang=en What are you going to do? The Postdoc is expected to primarily contribute to the analysis and writing of the shared output (existing datasets and new data), as well as to the coordination and carrying out of the field-work. Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 19 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time €4.251 - €4.422 Who are you? There are several consortium partners involved in the project. Ecosensys, Jasja Dekker, and GKA are mainly responsible for the implementation of the fieldwork and for data collection and management. The postdoctoral researcher is to be appointed at the University of Groningen (RUG) for three years at 0.8 FTE and will be responsible for project coordination, conducting the analyses, writing scientific reports, and, where necessary and desired, supporting the fieldwork activities of the consortium partners. Representatives of various consortium partners (Ecosensys, Jasja Dekker Ecologie, GKA, and RUG) take place in the PREDWEI 2 steering committee, which meets twice a year (before and after the field season) to discuss plans and review results.The Postdoc is expected to primarily contribute to the analysis and writing of the shared output (existing datasets and new data), as well as to the coordination and carrying out of the field-work. For the Postdoc position, we are looking for a motivated candidate with a PhD degree in the field(s) of ecology or equivalent, and a background and interest in conservation. The ideal candidate has excellent skills in the statistical analyses of large (spatial) ecological datasets, has demonstratable experience with setting up and analyses of data of cameratrap studies and telemetry / tracking data, is able to work independently while being a team player, and has proven scientific writing skills. The candidate will be based in the group of Prof. C. Smit (https://www.rug.nl/staff/c.smit/), for a period of 3 years (0.8 FTE). Ideally, the candidate is available from 1 December 2026 onwards. What can you expect from us? In accordance with the collective labor agreement for Dutch universities, we offer a salary of at least €                    4.251\n                    \n                    up to a maximum of €                    4.422                    (salary scale 10.4)\n                    gross per month for a full-time employment contract. 232 vacation hours per year, based on a 38-hour workweek (1.0 FTE). You can also work more or fewer hours in exchange for more or fewer free hours. For example, with a 40-hour workweek, you save 96 extra free hours, and with a 36-hour workweek, you lose 96 hours. End-of-year bonus of 8.3% and 8% holiday allowance. Extensive opportunities for personal and professional development. A fixed-term contract for the duration of 0.8 FTE for 36 months. Where will you be working? At the University of Groningen (UG), researchers from all fields of academia and technology are working on academic challenges and societal questions. Lecturers prepare their students for meaningful careers within or outside the academic world. Interdisciplinary research and teaching, sharing of knowledge, collaboration with businesses, government institutions, and societal organizations are aspects that are of the utmost importance to this European top university. The UG aims to be an open academic community with an inclusive and safe working climate that invites you to add your value. The Faculty of Science and Engineering (FSE) provides teaching and research across a wide range of disciplines, from physics and biology to artificial intelligence, mechanical engineering, and pharmacy. In close collaboration with partners from industry, healthcare, and society, we contribute to the urgent challenges of our time, such as energy, sustainability, digitization, and medical technology. Our community is open and informal, with more than 7,000 students, 1,000 PhD students, and 1,400 staff members from all over the world. If you would like to learn more about the Faculty of Science and Engineering, visit rug.nl/fse . The candidate will be based in the group of Prof. C. Smit (https://www.rug.nl/staff/c.smit/), for a period of 3 years (0.8 FTE). string(27) \"sollicitatieprocedure_wp_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n  }\n} Application procedure Step 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Step 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Step 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Step 4: Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture. Step 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen! Interested? Does this vacancy appeal to you? If so, click on the button below and apply straightaway. Please add the following documents to your application: CV Cover letter. Apply now Do you have any questions or need more information? Questions about the content of the job? Christian Smit Full Professor C.Smit@rug.nl Questions about your application process? Kimberley ter Voorde - Speelman Human Resources Assistant k.m.ter.voorde-speelman@rug.nl Information about applying When scheduling meetings, we will take your schedule into account as much as possible. The University of Groningen considers social safety important. We strive to be a university where staff and students feel respected and at home, regardless of differences in background, experiences, perspectives, and identity. For more information, see also our page about our diversity policy . Acquisition is not appreciated. Our selection procedure follows the guidelines of the NVP Application Code. Read document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Go straight to All vacancies Working at UG Contact information University of Groningen PO Box 72 9700 AB Groningen The Netherlands How to find us Follow us on array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
    },
    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/postdoc-public-perceptions-and-acceptability-of-hydrogen-developments-2503/?lang=en": {
      "title": "Postdoc Public perceptions and acceptability of Hydrogen Developments",
      "description": "Postdoc Public perceptions and acceptability of Hydrogen Developments - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts Postdoc Public perceptions and acceptability of Hydrogen Developments Apply now Post-doc Researcher Postdoc Public perceptions and acceptability of Hydrogen Developments This vacancy is only available in English Join us in this exciting and multidisciplinary endeavor to shape the future of hydrogen as a sustainable and socially accepted energy solution. Faculty of Behavioural and Social Sciences Apply no later than: 22 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time 0.9 FTE €3.706 - €5.760 Share this vacancy Postdoc Public perceptions and acceptability of Hydrogen Developments Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/postdoc-public-perceptions-and-acceptability-of-hydrogen-developments-2503/?lang=en What are you going to do? Hydrogen is a rapidly evolving development aimed at mitigating greenhouse gas emissions. Hydrogen is not an energy source in itself, but serves as an energy carrier. Energy produced from gas and/or renewable energy sources can be saved and stored in a form of hydrogen and used when needed. The development and implementation of hydrogen is a technological and, more importantly, a societal challenge. It is critical to gain understanding of how people form their perceptions and acceptability judgements of hydrogen projects, which key factors play a role in public perceptions and acceptability, and how to incorporate this knowledge in socially responsible policy-making. These questions are at the heart of this project. In this postdoc position, you will i) conduct large-scale longitudinal surveys to study the relationships between the identified factors and public perceptions and acceptability of hydrogen; ii) conduct experimental studies to infer the causal relationships between the identified factors and public acceptability of hydrogen; iii) give evidence-based recommendations for how to better incorporate public perceptions and acceptability in policy-making, and iv) carry out dissemination activities to communicate the findings to other professionals from science and practice, and the general population. Besides, the project implies collaboration with multiple other partners from science (different disciplines), industry, organizations, and government bodies. Faculty of Behavioural and Social Sciences Apply no later than: 22 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time €3.706 - €5.760 Who are you? We are looking for candidates who meet the following requirements The successful candidate should hold (or be close to obtaining) a PhD in Environmental Psychology or a related discipline and be familiar with Environmental psychology theories and research in energy and social science. Furthermore, the successful candidate should be comfortable working with quantitative empirical methods, including longitudinal survey and experimental methodologies, ideally with substantial prior experience. Finally, the successful candidate should have: experience working with large-scale datasets and projects involving multiple stakeholders. excellent command of the English language; ability to work independently and manage joint research activities; a team player with strong communication skills; demonstrable competences as conceptual capacity, environment orientation, presenting and result orientation. What can you expect from us? In accordance with the collective labor agreement for Dutch universities, we offer a salary of at least €                    3.706\n                    \n                    up to a maximum of €                    5.760                    (salary scale 10)\n                    gross per month for a full-time employment contract. 232 vacation hours per year, based on a 38-hour workweek (1.0 FTE). You can also work more or fewer hours in exchange for more or fewer free hours. For example, with a 40-hour workweek, you save 96 extra free hours, and with a 36-hour workweek, you lose 96 hours. End-of-year bonus of 8.3% and 8% holiday allowance. Extensive opportunities for personal and professional development. A temporary contract of 0.9 FTE for a period of 28 months. Where will you be working? At the University of Groningen (UG), researchers from all fields of academia and technology are working on academic challenges and societal questions. Lecturers prepare their students for meaningful careers within or outside the academic world. Interdisciplinary research and teaching, sharing of knowledge, collaboration with businesses, government institutions, and societal organizations are aspects that are of the utmost importance to this European top university. The UG aims to be an open academic community with an inclusive and safe working climate that invites you to add your value. The Faculty of Behavioural and Social Sciences (GMW) excels in research and teaching in the areas of behaviour, thinking, learning, and participation in society. More than 4,500 students and approximately 650 staff address social questions and challenges that people experience in daily life. Our core focus is on individual and societal resilience and how to strengthen it. We focus on current themes such as health and wellbeing, sustainable living, learning and development, inclusive society, safe and healthy upbringing, and work and collaboration. If you would like to learn more about the Faculty of Behavioural and Social Sciences, visit rug.nl/gmw . Environmental Psychology at the University of Groningen has a national and international reputation for excellence. Research within the Environmental Psychology group focuses on a wide range of topics, including understanding which factors influence sustainable behaviours (such as energy use, car use, food consumption); understanding how people cope with environmental and climate risks; understanding the effectiveness of strategies to promote sustainable behaviour; understanding the acceptability of environmental policies; and the effects of sustainable behaviour on wellbeing. The research contributes to theory development and to practice. The Environmental Psychology group collaborates with scholars from different disciplines within and outside the University of Groningen, as well as with governments, NGOs, businesses, and organisations. string(27) \"sollicitatieprocedure_wp_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n  }\n} Application procedure Step 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Step 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Step 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Step 4: Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture. Step 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen! Interested? Does this vacancy appeal to you? If so, click on the button below and apply straightaway. Please add the following documents to your application: CV Cover letter. Apply now Do you have any questions or need more information? Questions about the content of the job? Gonzalo Palomo Vélez Researcher g.f.palomo.velez@rug.nl Questions about your application process? Johanna Tinga Human Resources Adviser J.M.Tinga@rug.nl Information about applying When scheduling meetings, we will take your schedule into account as much as possible. The University of Groningen considers social safety important. We strive to be a university where staff and students feel respected and at home, regardless of differences in background, experiences, perspectives, and identity. For more information, see also our page about our diversity policy . Acquisition is not appreciated. Our selection procedure follows the guidelines of the NVP Application Code. Read document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Go straight to All vacancies Working at UG Contact information University of Groningen PO Box 72 9700 AB Groningen The Netherlands How to find us Follow us on array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
    },
    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/praktijkonderzoeker-regeneratieve-bedrijfsontwikkeling-landbouw-2519/?lang=en": {
      "title": "Praktijkonderzoeker regeneratieve bedrijfsontwikkeling landbouw",
      "description": "Praktijkonderzoeker regeneratieve bedrijfsontwikkeling landbouw - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts Praktijkonderzoeker regeneratieve bedrijfsontwikkeling landbouw Apply now Postdoctoraal onderzoeker Praktijkonderzoeker regeneratieve bedrijfsontwikkeling landbouw This vacancy is only available in Dutch Wil jij een actieve rol spelen in het vormgeven van een duurzame toekomst voor de landbouwsector? Wil je onderzoek, landbouwpraktijk en samenwerking met verschillende partijen met elkaar verbinden? Dan is dit jouw kans om deel uit te maken van het landelijke transitieprogramma regeneratieve landbouw (ReGeNL) bij de Faculteit Campus Fryslân van de Rijksuniversiteit Groningen. Campus Fryslân Apply no later than: 30 oktober 2026 0.8 - 1 FTE €3.706 - €5.760 Share this vacancy Praktijkonderzoeker regeneratieve bedrijfsontwikkeling landbouw Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/praktijkonderzoeker-regeneratieve-bedrijfsontwikkeling-landbouw-2519/?lang=en Wat ga je doen? Als praktijkonderzoeker werk je samen met boeren, begeleiders, onderzoekers, kennisinstellingen en ketenpartijen aan de transitie naar een duurzame en regeneratieve landbouw. Je draagt bij aan de begeleiding en ontwikkeling van circa 1.000 boeren en onderzoekt wat boeren en andere betrokkenen nodig hebben om stappen te zetten in hun bedrijfsontwikkeling. Je verbindt de landbouwpraktijk en onderzoek. Je haalt ervaringen, vragen en knelpunten uit de praktijk op, analyseert deze en vertaalt ze naar bruikbare inzichten en concrete vervolgstappen. Ook draag je bij aan de ontwikkeling en toepassing van nieuwe werkwijzen voor duurzame en regeneratieve bedrijfsontwikkeling. Je werkt in een dynamische omgeving waarin nog niet alles vastligt. Je krijgt ruimte om zelf initiatief te nemen, kansen te signaleren en samen met boeren, collega’s en partners te zoeken naar werkbare oplossingen. Jouw belangrijkste taken en verantwoordelijkheden Ondersteunen en begeleiden van boeren en ketenpartijen bij regeneratieve bedrijfsontwikkeling en transitieprocessen. Onderzoeken en analyseren van kansen, knelpunten en innovaties binnen de regeneratieve landbouw, en vertalen van inzichten uit de praktijk naar concrete oplossingen en handelingsperspectieven. Organiseren en faciliteren van kennisuitwisseling en samenwerking tussen boeren, begeleiders, onderzoekers, kennisinstellingen en andere ketenpartners. Monitoren, analyseren en rapporteren van de voortgang en resultaten van begeleidingstrajecten en het programma. Bijdragen aan de realisatie van de doelstellingen van het ReGeNL-programma en het tijdig opleveren van de beoogde resultaten. Je werkt dus niet alleen achter je bureau. Je bent regelmatig in gesprek met mensen uit de landbouwpraktijk, organiseert activiteiten, brengt partijen bij elkaar en zorgt dat signalen en ervaringen uit de praktijk hun weg vinden naar onderzoek en andersom. Campus Fryslân Apply no later than: 30 oktober 2026 €3.706 - €5.760 Wie ben jij? Voor deze functie zoeken we een nieuwsgierige en ondernemende collega die gemakkelijk verbinding maakt met verschillende typen mensen en graag werkt op het snijvlak van landbouwpraktijk, onderzoek en maatschappelijke transitie. Je beschikt over: een afgeronde universitaire masteropleiding, bijvoorbeeld in bedrijfskunde, economie, bestuurskunde, landbouw, (milieu)wetenschappen of een vergelijkbare richting; kennis van en/of affiniteit met de landbouwsector, duurzaamheid en duurzame transities; goede communicatieve en samenwerkingsvaardigheden en het vermogen om verschillende perspectieven en belangen met elkaar te verbinden; het vermogen om zelfstandig werkzaamheden te organiseren, prioriteiten te stellen en voortgang te bewaken; een ondernemende werkhouding met interesse in een omgeving waarin vraagstukken nog niet volledig zijn uitgekristalliseerd en waarin je samen met anderen naar werkbare oplossingen zoekt; een goede beheersing van het Nederlands en Engels, zowel mondeling als schriftelijk. Ervaring met praktijkonderzoek, projectcoördinatie, stakeholdermanagement, agrarischebedrijfsontwikkeling of de landbouwsector is een pré. Relevante werkervaring is gewenst, maar niet noodzakelijk. We vinden het vooral belangrijk dat je initiatief neemt, nieuwsgierig bent en gemakkelijk contact maakt met verschillende typen mensen. De toegevoegde waarde van deze functie zit in de combinatie van maatschappelijke impact, praktijkonderzoek en samenwerking met mensen uit de landbouwpraktijk. Impact maken Je draagt direct bij aan de transitie naar een duurzame en regeneratieve landbouw. Binnen het ReGeNL-programma worden circa 1.000 boeren begeleid bij veranderingen in hun bedrijfsvoering. Je ziet daarmee direct hoe jouw werk bijdraagt aan verandering in de landbouwpraktijk. Persoonlijke ontwikkeling Je ontwikkelt je verder op het gebied van praktijkonderzoek, coördinatie, stakeholdermanagement en transitiemanagement. Je krijgt ruimte om nieuwe verantwoordelijkheden op je te nemen en mee te groeien met nieuwe onderzoeks- en transitieprojecten. Dynamische werkomgeving Je werkt in een interdisciplinair en ondernemend team waarin nog niet alles vastligt. Er is ruimte voor initiatief, creativiteit, flexibiliteit en professionalisering. Breed netwerk Je krijgt toegang tot een breed netwerk van boeren, onderzoekers, kennisinstellingen, ketenpartijen en andere partners die werken aan de transitie van de landbouw. Werken op het snijvlak van praktijk en onderzoek Je brengt inzichten uit wetenschappelijk onderzoek en ervaringen uit de landbouwpraktijk bij elkaar en helpt deze te vertalen naar concrete handelingsperspectieven voor boeren en andere betrokkenen. Wat kan je van ons verwachten? Wij bieden, in overeenstemming met cao Nederlandse Universiteiten een salaris van minimaal €                    3.706\n                    \n                    tot maximaal €                    5.760                    (schaal 10)\n                    bruto per maand bij een fulltime dienstverband. 232 verlofuren per jaar, o.b.v. een 38-urige werkweek (1.0 fte). Je kunt ook meer of minder uren werken, in ruil voor meer of minder vrije uren. Zo spaar je bij een 40-urige werkweek 96 extra vrije uren en lever je bij een 36-urige werkweek 96 uur in. Eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3% en 8% vakantietoeslag. Uitgebreide mogelijkheden voor persoonlijke en professionele ontwikkeling. Een tijdelijke aanstelling van één jaar, met de mogelijkheid tot verlenging met drie jaar bij een positief resultaat- en ontwikkelgesprek.\nEen functieomvang van 0,8 – 1,0 fte. Waar ga je werken? Bij de Rijksuniversiteit Groningen (RUG) werken onderzoekers in alle takken van wetenschap en techniek aan wetenschappelijke uitdagingen en maatschappelijke vraagstukken. Docenten leiden hun studenten op voor een betekenisvolle loopbaan in de wetenschap of daarbuiten. Interdisciplinair onderzoek en onderwijs, kennis delen, participatie met bedrijven, overheidsinstellingen en maatschappelijke partijen staan bij deze top 100-universiteit hoog in het vaandel. De RUG wil een open academische gemeenschap zijn met een inclusief en veilig werkklimaat dat je uitnodigt om jouw waarde toe te voegen. Campus Fryslân (CF) is the eleventh and youngest faculty of the University of Groningen, located in Leeuwarden. With over 100 staff members, approximately 350 students, and 45 PhD students, it forms a small-scale community in which both working and studying is enjoyable. Students benefit from innovative teaching, and passionate researchers investigate global themes for which we seek local solutions. This aligns with our motto: Global challenges, local solutions . We collaborate with various regional, national, and international partners to connect teaching, research, and practice. Our teaching and research focus on the themes of Circular Society and Economy, Sustainable Environment and Wellbeing, and Responsible Governance and Technology. If you would like to learn more about Campus Fryslân, visit rug.nl/cf Deze functie is bij het Centrum voor Duurzame Landbouw Transitie (CDLT) van de Faculteit Campus Fryslân in Leeuwarden van de Rijksuniversiteit Groningen. De Rijksuniversiteit Groningen is internationaal georiënteerd en werkt aan complexe maatschappelijke vraagstukken en transities. Binnen het CDLT werken onderzoekers en praktijkpartners samen aan kennis, innovatie en concrete oplossingen voor de landbouw van de toekomst. Het CDLT is een kernpartner in het landelijke ReGeNL-programma en richt zich op hetbverbinden van landbouwpraktijk en wetenschappelijk onderzoek om de transitie naar een duurzame landbouw te versnellen. Daarbij staat leren vanuit de praktijk centraal: wat werkt, welke belemmeringen ervaren boeren en welke nieuwe routes kunnen bijdragen aan een duurzame landbouw? In deze vacature verstaan we onder duurzame landbouw een landbouw die ecologisch, economisch en sociaal toekomstbestendig is. Binnen het CDLT worden samen met boeren en partners verschillende routes onderzocht en ontwikkeld om deze transitie vorm te geven, waaronder vormen van regeneratieve landbouw. string(27) \"sollicitatieprocedure_wp_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n  }\n} Sollicitatieprocedure Stap 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Stap 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Stap 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Stap 4: Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture. Stap 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen! Interesse? Klinkt dit als een uitdaging die bij je past? Solliciteer dan direct via onderstaande knop! Voeg bij je sollicitatie de volgende documenten toe: CV Motivatiebrief. In je motivatie lezen we graag waarom je enthousiast wordt van het werken op het snijvlak van landbouwpraktijk, onderzoek en maatschappelijke transitie en welke ervaring, kennis en kwaliteiten je meebrengt die hierbij aansluiten. Solliciteer nu Heb je vragen of meer informatie nodig? Heb je vragen over de inhoud van de vacature? Ingrid van Huizen Projectmanager i.b.van.huizen@rug.nl Heb je vragen over de sollicitatieprocedure? Griet Vonk Projectleider g.g.vonk@rug.nl Informatie over solliciteren Bij de planning van de gesprekken houden wij zoveel mogelijk rekening met jouw agenda. De Rijksuniversiteit Groningen vindt sociale veiligheid belangrijk. We streven ernaar een universiteit te zijn waar medewerkers en studenten zich gerespecteerd en thuis voelen, ongeacht verschillen in achtergronden, ervaringen, perspectieven en identiteit. Voor meer informatie zie ook onze pagina over ons diversiteitsbeleid . Acquisitie wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Onze selectieprocedure volgt de richtlijnen van de NVP Sollicitatiecode Lees hier het document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Jump to Alle vacatures Werken bij RUG Contactinformatie Rijksuniversiteit Groningen Postbus 72 9700 AB Groningen Waar vindt u ons Volg ons op array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
    },
    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/postdoctoral-researcher-graphite-from-renewable-aromatic-hydrocarbons-2452/?lang=en": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral researcher: Graphite from Renewable Aromatic Hydrocarbons",
      "description": "Postdoctoral researcher: Graphite from Renewable Aromatic Hydrocarbons - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts Postdoctoral researcher: Graphite from Renewable Aromatic Hydrocarbons Apply now Post-doc Researcher Postdoctoral researcher: Graphite from Renewable Aromatic Hydrocarbons This vacancy is only available in English A postdoctoral position is available in the Green Chemical Reaction Engineering group of Prof. Peter J. Deuss, where the postdoc is expected to characterize and convert isolated and purified carbon streams to mesophase carbon and graphitic materials for carbon fibre applications. Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 18 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time 1 FTE €4.251 - €4.925 Share this vacancy Postdoctoral researcher: Graphite from Renewable Aromatic Hydrocarbons Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/postdoctoral-researcher-graphite-from-renewable-aromatic-hydrocarbons-2452/?lang=en What are you going to do? Graphite is considered a critical material for Europe because it is essential for strategic clean-tech and multiple industrial applications, while Europe is highly dependent on imports with concentrated supply risks. The Graphene project is a partnership between BioBTX, Teijin Europe, ISPT, the university of Groningen and the Hanze University of Applied Science, which aims to develop and optimize the production of graphite from side-streams from the BioBTX Integrated Cascading Catalytic Pyrolysis process based on waste plastics. Expected: Plan and execute experimental work based on the description above. Communicate finding to the project team in written report form and via presentations at project meetings. Participate in research activities within the research group, participating in general activities to keep the laboratory facilities running. Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 18 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time €4.251 - €4.925 Who are you? Required: PhD in Chemical or related sciences. Experience with carbon-based materials and their characterization. Knowledge of handling different reactor setups. Experience with working safely in a chemical laboratory environment. Good communication skills, orally and written. What can you expect from us? In accordance with the collective labor agreement for Dutch universities, we offer a salary of at least €                    4.251\n                                          (salary scale 10.4)                    \n                    up to a maximum of €                    4.925                    (salary scale 10.7)\n                    gross per month for a full-time employment contract. 232 vacation hours per year, based on a 38-hour workweek (1.0 FTE). You can also work more or fewer hours in exchange for more or fewer free hours. For example, with a 40-hour workweek, you save 96 extra free hours, and with a 36-hour workweek, you lose 96 hours. End-of-year bonus of 8.3% and 8% holiday allowance. Extensive opportunities for personal and professional development. A temporary contract of 5 months. Where will you be working? At the University of Groningen (UG), researchers from all fields of academia and technology are working on academic challenges and societal questions. Lecturers prepare their students for meaningful careers within or outside the academic world. Interdisciplinary research and teaching, sharing of knowledge, collaboration with businesses, government institutions, and societal organizations are aspects that are of the utmost importance to this European top university. The UG aims to be an open academic community with an inclusive and safe working climate that invites you to add your value. The Faculty of Science and Engineering (FSE) provides teaching and research across a wide range of disciplines, from physics and biology to artificial intelligence, mechanical engineering, and pharmacy. In close collaboration with partners from industry, healthcare, and society, we contribute to the urgent challenges of our time, such as energy, sustainability, digitization, and medical technology. Our community is open and informal, with more than 7,000 students, 1,000 PhD students, and 1,400 staff members from all over the world. If you would like to learn more about the Faculty of Science and Engineering, visit rug.nl/fse . You will be working in the Green Chemical Reaction Engineering chemical Laboratories of the Engineering & Technology Institute Groningen of the University of Groningen at the Zernike Campus. string(27) \"sollicitatieprocedure_wp_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n  }\n} Application procedure Step 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Step 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Step 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Step 4: Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture. Step 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen! Interested? Does this vacancy appeal to you? If so, click on the button below and apply straightaway. Please add the following documents to your application: CV. Cover letter. Apply now Do you have any questions or need more information? Questions about the content of the job? Peter Deuss Full Professor P.J.Deuss@rug.nl Questions about your application process? Peter Deuss Full Professor P.J.Deuss@rug.nl Information about applying When scheduling meetings, we will take your schedule into account as much as possible. The University of Groningen considers social safety important. We strive to be a university where staff and students feel respected and at home, regardless of differences in background, experiences, perspectives, and identity. For more information, see also our page about our diversity policy . Acquisition is not appreciated. Our selection procedure follows the guidelines of the NVP Application Code. Read document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Go straight to All vacancies Working at UG Contact information University of Groningen PO Box 72 9700 AB Groningen The Netherlands How to find us Follow us on array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
    },
    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/onderzoeker-gronings-perspectief-2512/?lang=en": {
      "title": "Onderzoeker Gronings Perspectief",
      "description": "Onderzoeker Gronings Perspectief - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts Onderzoeker Gronings Perspectief Apply now Postdoctoraal onderzoeker Onderzoeker Gronings Perspectief This vacancy is only available in Dutch Als onderzoeker maak je deel uit van een onderzoeksteam, met daarin onderzoekers van de Rijksuniversiteit Groningen (RUG) en onderzoekers van het Nivel. Gezamenlijk dragen de onderzoekers zorg voor alle onderdelen van het onderzoek. Gronings Perspectief is een onderzoek in een complexe maatschappelijke context. De onderzoeker zal als onderdeel van het onderzoeksteam meedenken over de theoretische maar ook zeker de praktische implicaties van het onderzoek. De onderzoeker valt hiërarchisch onder de basiseenheid Sociale Psychologie. Faculteit Gedrags- & Maatschappijwetenschappen Apply no later than: 18 oktober 2026 0.6 FTE €3.706 - €4.925 Share this vacancy Onderzoeker Gronings Perspectief Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/onderzoeker-gronings-perspectief-2512/?lang=en Wat ga je doen? De onderzoeker werkt mee aan Gronings Perspectief. Gronings Perspectief is een onderzoeksproject waarmee sinds 2016 de impact van de gaswinning op de inwoners van de provincie Groningen in kaart wordt gebracht. Een belangrijke pijler van het onderzoek zijn periodieke metingen onder een panel van bewoners. Met deze metingen wordt de impact van de gevolgen van de gaswinning op “kernvariabelen” onderzocht, waaronder geestelijke en fysieke gezondheid, veiligheidsgevoelens, risicobeleving en vertrouwen in overheden, instanties en de toekomst. Daarnaast worden interviews uitgevoerd met onder meer bewoners en professionals om inzicht te krijgen in het verhaal achter de cijfers. Het onderzoek wordt gefinancierd door het ministerie van Binnenlandse Zaken en Koninkrijksrelaties. De onderzoekers voeren hun werk onafhankelijk uit en stemmen af met een begeleidingscommissie waarin de belangen van bewoners, lokale, regionale en landelijke overheden en instanties zijn vertegenwoordigd. Het onderzoek wordt uitgevoerd door een team, bestaande uit onderzoekers van de RUG en onderzoekers van Nivel. De onderzoekers hebben onlangs subsidie toegekend gekregen voor een verlenging van het onderzoeksproject van vier jaar, voor de periode 2027 tot en met 2030. We zoeken voor deze fase een onderzoeker die zich met name zal bezighouden met de kwalitatieve onderdelen van het onderzoek, namelijk interviews met bewoners en professionals in de provincie Groningen. De onderzoeker zal zelfstandig werken aan het ontwikkelen van itemlijsten, het contact leggen met respondenten, het afnemen van interviews en de analyse en rapportage. De onderzoeker wordt tevens gevraagd mee te denken over de kwantitatieve onderdelen van het onderzoek (m.n.vragenlijstontwikkeling) en de codering van open vragen in de panelstudies. Ook zal de onderzoeker het voortouw nemen in het schrijven van publicaties voor wetenschappelijke tijdschriften. Faculteit Gedrags- & Maatschappijwetenschappen Apply no later than: 18 oktober 2026 €3.706 - €4.925 Wie ben jij? Wij zoeken kandidaten die aan de volgende eisen voldoen: Afgerond Masterdiploma in Sociale Wetenschappen (of een verwante discipline). Ruime aantoonbare ervaring met het zelfstandig opzetten en uitvoeren van kwalitatief sociaalwetenschappelijk onderzoek, waaronder het ontwikkelen van interviewleidraden, het afnemen van diepte-interviews, het systematisch verwerken en inhoudelijk interpreteren van kwalitatieve gegevens en het toegankelijk rapporteren hierover. Vaardigheid in het analyseren van kwalitatieve interviewdata met behulp van gespecialiseerde software. Ervaring met het verbinden van kwalitatieve en kwantitatieve onderzoeksresultaten. Goede verbale en schriftelijke vaardigheden in het Nederlands en het Engels. Een teamspeler met sterke communicatieve vaardigheden. Kennis over de gaswinningsproblematiek en de impact hiervan op bewoners en professionals in de regio. Ervaring met het interviewen van respondenten in de context van de gaswinningsproblematiek is een pre. Wat kan je van ons verwachten? Wij bieden, in overeenstemming met cao Nederlandse Universiteiten een salaris van minimaal €                    3.706\n                                          (schaal 10)                    \n                    tot maximaal €                    4.925                    (schaal 10.7)\n                    bruto per maand bij een fulltime dienstverband. 232 verlofuren per jaar, o.b.v. een 38-urige werkweek (1.0 fte). Je kunt ook meer of minder uren werken, in ruil voor meer of minder vrije uren. Zo spaar je bij een 40-urige werkweek 96 extra vrije uren en lever je bij een 36-urige werkweek 96 uur in. Eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3% en 8% vakantietoeslag. Uitgebreide mogelijkheden voor persoonlijke en professionele ontwikkeling. Een tijdelijk dienstverband met een omvang van 0,6 fte voor de duur van 4 jaar. Functie-indeling in het UFO-functieprofiel van Onderzoeker 4.\nIngangsdatum: 1 december 2026 Waar ga je werken? Bij de Rijksuniversiteit Groningen (RUG) werken onderzoekers in alle takken van wetenschap en techniek aan wetenschappelijke uitdagingen en maatschappelijke vraagstukken. Docenten leiden hun studenten op voor een betekenisvolle loopbaan in de wetenschap of daarbuiten. Interdisciplinair onderzoek en onderwijs, kennis delen, participatie met bedrijven, overheidsinstellingen en maatschappelijke partijen staan bij deze top 100-universiteit hoog in het vaandel. De RUG wil een open academische gemeenschap zijn met een inclusief en veilig werkklimaat dat je uitnodigt om jouw waarde toe te voegen. The Faculty of Behavioural and Social Sciences (GMW) excels in research and teaching in the areas of behaviour, thinking, learning, and participation in society. More than 4,500 students and approximately 650 staff address social questions and challenges that people experience in daily life. Our core focus is on individual and societal resilience and how to strengthen it. We focus on current themes such as health and wellbeing, sustainable living, learning and development, inclusive society, safe and healthy upbringing, and work and collaboration. If you would like to learn more about the Faculty of Behavioural and Social Sciences, visit rug.nl/gmw . Extra informatie https://www.groningsperspectief.nl/ Sociale Psychologie string(27) \"sollicitatieprocedure_wp_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n  }\n} Sollicitatieprocedure Stap 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Stap 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Stap 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Stap 4: Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture. Stap 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen! Interesse? Klinkt dit als een uitdaging die bij je past? Solliciteer dan direct via onderstaande knop! Voeg bij je sollicitatie de volgende documenten toe: CV. Motivatiebrief. De selectiegesprekken vinden plaats op maandag 26 oktober 2026. Solliciteer nu Heb je vragen of meer informatie nodig? Heb je vragen over de inhoud van de vacature? Michel Dückers Externe medewerker m.l.a.duckers@rug.nl Heb je vragen over de sollicitatieprocedure? Michel Dückers Externe medewerker m.l.a.duckers@rug.nl Informatie over solliciteren Bij de planning van de gesprekken houden wij zoveel mogelijk rekening met jouw agenda. De Rijksuniversiteit Groningen vindt sociale veiligheid belangrijk. We streven ernaar een universiteit te zijn waar medewerkers en studenten zich gerespecteerd en thuis voelen, ongeacht verschillen in achtergronden, ervaringen, perspectieven en identiteit. Voor meer informatie zie ook onze pagina over ons diversiteitsbeleid . Acquisitie wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Onze selectieprocedure volgt de richtlijnen van de NVP Sollicitatiecode Lees hier het document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Jump to Alle vacatures Werken bij RUG Contactinformatie Rijksuniversiteit Groningen Postbus 72 9700 AB Groningen Waar vindt u ons Volg ons op array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
