    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/docent-frans-2488/?lang=en": {
      "title": "Docent Frans",
      "description": "Docent Frans - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts Teacher French language learning Apply now Docent Teacher French language learning The University of Groningen is a research university with a strong international outlook. It is socially engaged and deeply connected to its local community. Researchers and lecturers across a wide range of disciplines pursue their work with a passion for scholarship. The university empowers everyone to achieve their full potential, actively fostering the talent, ambition, and achievements of both students and staff. Quality has been central to the university for 400 years—and with great success: it consistently ranks among the top 100 universities worldwide. Faculty and Degree Programme The Faculty of Arts builds upon a four-century-old tradition. Our mission is to be an ambitious, leading faculty in education and high-quality research, characterized by a strong international orientation and deep roots in the Northern Netherlands. We create and share knowledge through excellence in teaching and research. We educate over 5,000 Dutch and international students within a modern, broad-based, and international institution, producing future-oriented, articulate, and intellectually independent graduates. Faculty of Arts Apply no later than: 12 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time 0.35 FTE €3.706 - €5.760 Share this vacancy Teacher French language learning Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/docent-frans-2488/?lang=en What are you going to do? Je bereidt taalvaardigheidscursussen Frans voor, overziet deze, organiseert ze en geeft ze volgens de methode die is ontwikkeld door het Language Learning Team van het ETC, zoals beschreven in onze missieverklaring . Daarnaast werk je nauw samen met andere collega’s binnen de opleiding Europese Talen en Culturen, aan de verdere ontwikkeling van onze aanpak. Kijk hier voor meer informatie over het programma . Faculty of Arts Apply no later than: 12 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time €3.706 - €5.760 Who are you? You have a command of the French language at the C1/C2 level. You hold a master’s degree in the humanities, e.g., in linguistics, literature, cultural studies, or history, or a Master of Education. Ideally, you have relevant experience in an academic FLE context: teaching courses up to the B1 level teaching through tasks, following usage-based and CLIL principles creating evidence-based and research-based teaching materials based on the CEFR. using digital tools to enhance your face-to-face teaching experience organizing virtual exchanges is a plus. You enjoy working both independently and as part of a team and producing high-quality work. Your strengths include pedagogical creativity, team spirit, autonomy, entrepreneurship, communication, and efficient organization. You can communicate and participate in meetings in English (CEFR C1 level in reading, listening, writing, and speaking). The interviews will most likely take place on 15 and 16 October 2026. What can you expect from us? In accordance with the collective labor agreement for Dutch universities, we offer a salary of at least €                    3.706\n                    \n                    up to a maximum of €                    5.760                    (salary scale 10)\n                    gross per month for a full-time employment contract. 232 vacation hours per year, based on a 38-hour workweek (1.0 FTE). You can also work more or fewer hours in exchange for more or fewer free hours. For example, with a 40-hour workweek, you save 96 extra free hours, and with a 36-hour workweek, you lose 96 hours. End-of-year bonus of 8.3% and 8% holiday allowance. Extensive opportunities for personal and professional development. This is a temporary 4 month position, due to sick leave replacement. The startdate is November 1, 2026; the enddate is February 28, 2027. Where will you be working? At the University of Groningen (UG), researchers from all fields of academia and technology are working on academic challenges and societal questions. Lecturers prepare their students for meaningful careers within or outside the academic world. Interdisciplinary research and teaching, sharing of knowledge, collaboration with businesses, government institutions, and societal organizations are aspects that are of the utmost importance to this European top university. The UG aims to be an open academic community with an inclusive and safe working climate that invites you to add your value. The Faculty of Arts is a large and dynamic faculty located in the heart of the city of Groningen. More than 5,500 students and 900 staff work every day at the frontiers of knowledge. The Faculty offers a diverse range of academic programmes, with 16 Bachelor’s programmes and over 40 Master’s programmes. With its strong international orientation, the Faculty conducts research in fields including archaeology, cultural studies, history, international relations, journalism, literature, and linguistics. If you would like to learn more about the Faculty of Arts, visit rug.nl/let . Students in the BA European Languages ??and Cultures (ELC) programme choose a specialization track—Language and Society, Culture and Literature, or Politics and Society—combined with one of eight languages. In addition to German, these include Dutch as a Second Language (NT2), English, French, Italian, Russian, Spanish, and Swedish. The language programmes build on the expertise of a motivated international team of language instructors, ensuring that language acquisition is fully integrated with learning about the target language and culture. At ELC, we employ effective, research-based teaching methods and the latest technological innovations to support language learning and to strengthen our students’ profiles as future language ambassadors and cultural mediators for Europe. string(27) \"sollicitatieprocedure_wp_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n  }\n} Sollicitatieprocedure Stap 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Stap 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Stap 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Stap 4: Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture. Stap 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen! Interested? Does this vacancy appeal to you? If so, click on the button below and apply straightaway. Please add the following documents to your application: CV. Cover letter. The job interviews will take place on 15 and 16 October 2026. Apply now Do you have any questions or need more information? Questions about the content of the job? Anja Schüppert Associate Professor A.Schueppert@rug.nl Questions about your application process? Sanna Buurke Head of Department M.S.D.Buurke@rug.nl Information about applying When scheduling meetings, we will take your schedule into account as much as possible. The University of Groningen considers social safety important. We strive to be a university where staff and students feel respected and at home, regardless of differences in background, experiences, perspectives, and identity. For more information, see also our page about our diversity policy . Acquisition is not appreciated. Our selection procedure follows the guidelines of the NVP Application Code. Read document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Go straight to All vacancies Working at UG Contact information University of Groningen PO Box 72 9700 AB Groningen The Netherlands How to find us Follow us on array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
    },
    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/postdoc-in-energy-based-learning-of-dynamical-systems-2444/?lang=en": {
      "title": "Postdoc in Energy-based Learning of Dynamical Systems",
      "description": "Postdoc in Energy-based Learning of Dynamical Systems - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts Postdoc in Energy-based Learning of Dynamical Systems Apply now Post-doc Researcher Postdoc in Energy-based Learning of Dynamical Systems This vacancy is only available in English The University of Groningen is seeking a highly motivated postdoctoral researcher to work on systems theory for energy-based learning. Faculty of Science and Engineering 0.8 - 1 FTE €4.251 - €4.599 Share this vacancy Postdoc in Energy-based Learning of Dynamical Systems Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/postdoc-in-energy-based-learning-of-dynamical-systems-2444/?lang=en What are you going to do? As a postdoctoral researcher, you will develop and analyse new algorithms for energy-based learning of complex systems. A special emphasis will be placed on developing theory that goes beyond the steady-state behavior of dynamical systems. You will also have the opportunity to collaborate with PhD students working on adjacent topics within the same line of research. Faculty of Science and Engineering €4.251 - €4.599 Who are you? You should have: –  A PhD degree in optimization or systems and control theory. –  A strong mathematical background and an interest in conducting theoretical research. –  A proven track record. –  Excellent English communication skills, both written and spoken. What can you expect from us? In accordance with the collective labor agreement for Dutch universities, we offer a salary of at least €                    4.251\n                                          (salary scale 10.4)                    \n                    up to a maximum of €                    4.599                    (salary scale 10.5)\n                    gross per month for a full-time employment contract. 232 vacation hours per year, based on a 38-hour workweek (1.0 FTE). You can also work more or fewer hours in exchange for more or fewer free hours. For example, with a 40-hour workweek, you save 96 extra free hours, and with a 36-hour workweek, you lose 96 hours. End-of-year bonus of 8.3% and 8% holiday allowance. Extensive opportunities for personal and professional development. a holiday allowance of 8% gross annual income and an 8.3% year-end bonus\na full-time position (1.0 FTE) for 2 years Where will you be working? At the University of Groningen (UG), researchers from all fields of academia and technology are working on academic challenges and societal questions. Lecturers prepare their students for meaningful careers within or outside the academic world. Interdisciplinary research and teaching, sharing of knowledge, collaboration with businesses, government institutions, and societal organizations are aspects that are of the utmost importance to this European top university. The UG aims to be an open academic community with an inclusive and safe working climate that invites you to add your value. The Faculty of Science and Engineering (FSE) provides teaching and research across a wide range of disciplines, from physics and biology to artificial intelligence, mechanical engineering, and pharmacy. In close collaboration with partners from industry, healthcare, and society, we contribute to the urgent challenges of our time, such as energy, sustainability, digitization, and medical technology. Our community is open and informal, with more than 7,000 students, 1,000 PhD students, and 1,400 staff members from all over the world. If you would like to learn more about the Faculty of Science and Engineering, visit rug.nl/fse . The successful candidate will join the Bernoulli Institute for Mathematics, Computer Science and Artificial Intelligence within the Faculty of Science and Engineering at the University of Groningen. The research will be carried out in the Systems, Control and Optimization Group. The successful candidate will also benefit from connections within the Jan C. Willems Center for Systems and Control, including regular seminars, joint group meetings, and interaction with other postdocs and PhD students in a lively and supportive environment. The postdoc project is embedded within the European Research Council (ERC) Starting Grant project “Energy-based learning of complex dynamical systems” (E-BLOCS), led by Dr. Henk van Waarde. The postdoc will actively work together with the other members of the project, and also has many opportunities for international collaboration, research visits, and interdisciplinary training. string(27) \"sollicitatieprocedure_wp_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n  }\n} Application procedure Step 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Step 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Step 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Step 4: Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture. Step 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen! Interested? Does this vacancy appeal to you? If so, click on the button below and apply straightaway. Please add the following documents to your application: Motivation letter (1-2 pages) Curriculum Vitae Contact details of two academic references A representative publication Apply now Do you have any questions or need more information? Questions about the content of the job? Henk van Waarde Assistant Professor H.J.van.Waarde@rug.nl Questions about your application process? Henk van Waarde Assistant Professor H.J.van.Waarde@rug.nl Information about applying When scheduling meetings, we will take your schedule into account as much as possible. The University of Groningen considers social safety important. We strive to be a university where staff and students feel respected and at home, regardless of differences in background, experiences, perspectives, and identity. For more information, see also our page about our diversity policy . Acquisition is not appreciated. Our selection procedure follows the guidelines of the NVP Application Code. Read document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Go straight to All vacancies Working at UG Contact information University of Groningen PO Box 72 9700 AB Groningen The Netherlands How to find us Follow us on array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
    },
    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/phd-in-adapative-regulatory-frameworks-for-the-hydrogen-economy-2420/?lang=en": {
      "title": "PhD in Adapative Regulatory Frameworks for the Hydrogen Economy",
      "description": "PhD in Adapative Regulatory Frameworks for the Hydrogen Economy - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts PhD in Adapative Regulatory Frameworks for the Hydrogen Economy Apply now PhD PhD in Adapative Regulatory Frameworks for the Hydrogen Economy Are you an enthusiastic lawyer and/or public administration scholar with a curious research mind? Would you like to use your expertise to make a direct contribution to one of the major societal challenges of our time: the energy transition? Then we are looking for you! Faculty of Law Apply no later than: 11 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time €3.204 - €4.051 Share this vacancy PhD in Adapative Regulatory Frameworks for the Hydrogen Economy Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/phd-in-adapative-regulatory-frameworks-for-the-hydrogen-economy-2420/?lang=en What are you going to do? As a PhD candidate, you will investigate how the regulation of the hydrogen economy can be designed in such a way that the law is better able to evolve alongside the economic sector and society that it seeks to regulate than is currently the case. The legal framework governing the energy transition often has a “static” character. It regulates what exists rather than what could exist. In a sector in which innovation is still developing rapidly, such as the hydrogen economy, a static legal framework can have a constraining effect on the development of the economy and society. An adaptive legal framework can prevent this problem, but it is not yet known what such a framework should entail or which adaptive instruments can effectively support the development of the hydrogen economy rather than constrain it. Within an ongoing research project, we are developing a theory of an adaptive legal framework for the hydrogen economy. In this project, we aim to empirically test this theoretical framework in order to determine which interpretation and application of the theory can be effective in practice. In this research, theory will be translated into verifiable hypotheses concerning governance and regulatory instruments for the hydrogen economy. These hypotheses will be tested both quantitatively, on the basis of experiments, and qualitatively, through semi-structured interviews. In developing this research, you will become part of an interdisciplinary research team within the HySuccess programme of GroenvermogenNL, in which you will work together with colleagues from different universities and disciplines. Faculty of Law Apply no later than: 11 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time €3.204 - €4.051 Who are you? You are a connector; that is, you gain energy from initiating and fostering collaboration with and between partners. You hold a Masters degree, preferably in energy law. You have experience conducting empirical research. You have knowledge of and experience with European law. Knowledge of Dutch law is considered an advantage. Proficiency in the Dutch language is considered an advantage. You have a pragmatic attitude and are able to familiarise yourself with new areas of law. You have a sharp legal mind, determination, and the drive to make complex matters accessible. What can you expect from us? In accordance with the collective labor agreement for Dutch universities, we offer a salary of at least €                    3.204\n                    \n                    up to a maximum of €                    4.051                    (promovendus)\n                    gross per month for a full-time employment contract. 232 vacation hours per year, based on a 38-hour workweek (1.0 FTE). You can also work more or fewer hours in exchange for more or fewer free hours. For example, with a 40-hour workweek, you save 96 extra free hours, and with a 36-hour workweek, you lose 96 hours. End-of-year bonus of 8.3% and 8% holiday allowance. Extensive opportunities for personal and professional development. Temporary appointment for 1,0 fte for 4 years, with a in-between evaluation after 1,5 years (go-no go moment). Where will you be working? At the University of Groningen (UG), researchers from all fields of academia and technology are working on academic challenges and societal questions. Lecturers prepare their students for meaningful careers within or outside the academic world. Interdisciplinary research and teaching, sharing of knowledge, collaboration with businesses, government institutions, and societal organizations are aspects that are of the utmost importance to this European top university. The UG aims to be an open academic community with an inclusive and safe working climate that invites you to add your value. The Faculty of Law is a broad-based faculty. Our community is characterized by an open and informal atmosphere and consists of approximately 4,500 students and 400 staff. We foster an environment that combines academic tradition and innovation, in a way that addresses national and international societal issues. Our research and teaching are groundbreaking, with special attention paid to current themes such as sustainability and energy, technological developments including AI, and the democratic rule of law. We prepare legal professionals to adopt a broad perspective, think critically, and adapt to a rapidly changing world. We place a strong emphasis on the development of both students and staff. We actively seek connection across legal fields and disciplines, and with partners within and outside academia. If you would like to learn more about the Faculty of Law, visit rug.nl/rechten . You will be employed by the University of Groningen on a full-time basis (1.0 FTE). Initially, you will work closely with the PhD candidate appointed at Erasmus University Rotterdam, and subsequently together with the other partners within HySuccess. At the University of Groningen, you will join the Energy Law section, which is part of the Groningen Centre for Energy Law and Sustainability (GCELS). GCELS brings together legal expertise from all areas of law within the Faculty of Law and focuses on research and education relating to the energy transition. Its research covers the entire energy chain, from production, transport and storage to supply, and encompasses topics such as renewable energy, security of energy supply, climate policy and environmental protection. string(27) \"sollicitatieprocedure_wp_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n  }\n} Sollicitatieprocedure Stap 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Stap 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Stap 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Stap 4: Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture. Stap 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen! Interested? Does this vacancy appeal to you? If so, click on the button below and apply straightaway. Please add the following documents to your application: CV Cover letter. Apply now Do you have any questions or need more information? Questions about the content of the job? Lorenzo Squintani Full Professor L.Squintani@rug.nl Questions about your application process? Lorenzo Squintani Full Professor L.Squintani@rug.nl Information about applying When scheduling meetings, we will take your schedule into account as much as possible. The University of Groningen considers social safety important. We strive to be a university where staff and students feel respected and at home, regardless of differences in background, experiences, perspectives, and identity. For more information, see also our page about our diversity policy . Acquisition is not appreciated. Our selection procedure follows the guidelines of the NVP Application Code. Read document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Go straight to All vacancies Working at UG Contact information University of Groningen PO Box 72 9700 AB Groningen The Netherlands How to find us Follow us on array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
